{"parentUuid":"f2ebc65d-b1d4-459f-9a53-1401848334c8","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8c888221-02b0-4e51-9d65-3c44adc1a85c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E2Ei7Bc29uY82HSbu8w3y2","type":"tool_result","content":"why 0 0.45 7.523 | Most interfaces are cut for “users aged twenty-five to thirty-four.” Nobody in that bracket has taste. A person does.\nmeasure 8.733 9.183 9.326 | Baste starts with one person: the films they rewatch, the music they work to, the rooms they feel at home in, and the things they can’t stand in an app.\nfitting 19.267 19.717 6.87 | Then it fits an interface to them. Same screen, three people. The layout, the type, the colour and the motion all change.\nbaste 27.367 27.817 8.725 | To find a direction, Baste tries dozens of loose versions, warm and cool, sparse and dense, and a vision judge looks at every one.\nfit 37.3 37.75 6.504 | It keeps the best in each region, not one winner. So you see the real range of options before anything is final.\ncut 45.033 45.483 8.673 | What comes out is ready to use: images, vector icons, ambient loops, and design tokens for CSS, Tailwind or Panda.\ntalk 54.933 55.383 7.758 | And you can ask the persona why. They’ll tell you, in their own words, what they love and what would make a design feel like theirs.\nyours 63.9 64.35 4.206 | Bring your own people. Measure them in the Studio, and cut something that fits.\n\nWEBVTT\n\n1\n00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:03.660\nMost interfaces are cut for “users aged twenty-five to\n\n2\n00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:04.720\nthirty-four.”\n\n3\n00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:06.700\nNobody in that bracket has taste.\n\n4\n00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.890\nA person does.\n\n5\n00:00:09.213 --> 00:00:10.793\nBaste starts with one person:\n\n6\n00:00:10.813 --> 00:00:12.373\nthe films they rewatch,\n\n7\n00:00:12.393 --> 00:00:13.793\nthe music they work to,\n\n8\n00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:15.713\nthe rooms they feel at home in,\n\n9\n00:00:15.733 --> 00:00:18.543\nand the things they can’t stand in an app.\n\n10\n00:00:19.747 --> 00:00:21.547\nThen it fits an interface to them.\n\n11\n00:00:21.567 --> 00:00:23.247\nSame screen, three people.\n\n12\n00:00:23.267 --> 00:00:24.167\nThe layout, the type,\n\n13\n00:00:24.187 --> 00:00:26.377\nthe colour and the motion all change.\n\n14\n00:00:27.847 --> 00:00:28.827\nTo find a direction,\n\n15\n00:00:28.847 --> 00:00:31.767\nBaste tries dozens of loose versions,\n\n16\n00:00:31.787 --> 00:00:34.187\nwarm and cool, sparse and dense,\n\n17\n00:00:34.207 --> 00:00:36.357\nand a vision judge looks at every one.\n\n18\n00:00:37.780 --> 00:00:39.380\nIt keeps the best in each region,\n\n19\n00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:40.710\nnot one winner.\n\n20\n00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:42.700\nSo you see the real range of options before\n\n21\n00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:44.170\nanything is final.\n\n22\n00:00:45.513 --> 00:00:47.373\nWhat comes out is ready to use:\n\n23\n00:00:47.393 --> 00:00:50.293\nimages, vector icons, ambient loops,\n\n24\n00:00:50.313 --> 00:00:52.513\nand design tokens for CSS,\n\n25\n00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:54.083\nTailwind or Panda.\n\n26\n00:00:55.413 --> 00:00:57.293\nAnd you can ask the persona why.\n\n27\n00:00:57.313 --> 00:00:59.093\nThey’ll tell you, in their own words,\n\n28\n00:00:59.113 --> 00:01:01.453\nwhat they love and what would make a design\n\n29\n00:01:01.473 --> 00:01:03.063\nfeel like theirs.\n\n30\n00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:05.460\nBring your own people.\n\n31\n00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:06.940\nMeasure them in the Studio,\n\n32\n00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:08.550\nand cut something that fits.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d4bce1a9-4d1d-4f7f-bcfd-c8e0536b739f","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:40:51.864Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"why 0 0.45 7.523 | Most interfaces are cut for “users aged twenty-five to thirty-four.” Nobody in that bracket has taste. A person does.\nmeasure 8.733 9.183 9.326 | Baste starts with one person: the films they rewatch, the music they work to, the rooms t