{"parentUuid":"f5c53b77-be0f-40ab-944c-7efe02772613","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8c888221-02b0-4e51-9d65-3c44adc1a85c","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DfAMysYwZY4GDnWFBbu841","type":"tool_result","content":"WEBVTT\n\n00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:08.000\nCommencez par un persona. Fitting traduit son univers en couleurs, en typographie et en interface.\n\n00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:14.200\nDans Material, ajustez le tissu. Vos modifications restent dans ce navigateur.\n\n00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:19.200\nTokens contient le système de design. OpenPencil se trouve ici aussi.\n\n00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.640\nRassemblez vos références et vos notes dans Moodboard.\n\n00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.160\nDans Taste, indiquez ce qui vous plaît, et pourquoi.\n     1\tMost interfaces are cut for\n     2\t“users aged twenty-five to thirty-four.”\n     3\tNobody in that bracket has taste.\n     4\tA person does.\n     5\tBaste starts with one person:\n     6\tthe films they rewatch,\n     7\tthe music they work to,\n     8\tthe rooms they feel at home in,\n     9\tand the things they can’t stand in an app.\n    10\tThen it fits an interface to them.\n    11\tSame screen, three people.\n    12\tThe layout, the type,\n    13\tthe colour and the motion all change.\n    14\tTo find a direction,\n    15\tBaste tries dozens of loose versions,\n    16\twarm and cool, sparse and dense,\n    17\tand a vision judge looks at every one.\n    18\tIt keeps the best in each region,\n    19\tnot one winner.\n    20\tSo you see the real range of options\n    21\tbefore anything is final.\n    22\tWhat comes out is ready to use:\n    23\timages, vector icons, ambient loops,\n    24\tand design tokens for CSS,\n    25\tTailwind or Panda.\n    26\tAnd you can ask the persona why.\n    27\tThey’ll tell you, in their own words,\n    28\twhat they love\n    29\tand what would make a design feel like theirs.\n    30\tBring your own people.\n    31\tMeasure them in the Studio,\n    32\tand cut something that fits.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"0c00487c-95a7-47b0-9b01-d152e0beedd3","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:41:38.301Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"WEBVTT\n\n00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:08.000\nCommencez par un persona. Fitting traduit son univers en couleurs, en typographie et en interface.\n\n00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:14.200\nDans Material, ajustez le tissu. Vos modifications restent dans ce navigateur.\n\n00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:19.200\nTokens contient le système de design. OpenPencil se trouve ici aussi.\n\n00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:24.640\nRassemblez vos références et vos notes dans Moodboard.\n\n00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:29.160\nDans Taste, indiquez ce qui vous plaît, et pourquoi.\n     1\tMost interfaces are cut for\n     2\t“users aged twenty-five to thirty-four.”\n     3\tNobody in that bracket has taste.\n     4\tA person does.\n     5\tBaste starts with one person:\n     6\tthe films they rewatch,\n     7\tthe music they work to,\n     8\tthe rooms they feel at home in,\n     9\tand the things they can’t stand in an app.\n    10\tThen it fits an interface to them.\n    11\tSame screen, three people.\n    12\tThe layout, the type,\n    13\tthe colour and the motion all change.\n    14\tTo find a direction,\n    15\tBaste tries dozens of loose versions,\n    16\twarm and cool, sparse and dense,\n    17\tand a vision judge looks at every one.\n    18\tIt keeps the best in each region,\n    19\tnot one winner.\n    20\tSo you see the real range of options\n    21\tbefore anything is final.\n    22\tWhat comes out is ready to use:\n    23\timages, vector icons, ambient loops,\n    24\tand design tokens for CSS,\n    25\tTailwind or Panda.\n    26\tAnd you can ask the persona why.\n    27\tThey’ll tell you, in their own words,\n    28\twhat they love\n    29\tand what would make a design feel like theirs.\n    30\tBring your own people.\n    31\tMeasure them in the Studio,\n    32\tand cut something that fits.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f5c53b77-be0f-40ab-944c-7efe02772613","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"0c00487c-95a7-47b0-9b01-d152e0beedd3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"environment","snapshot":{"workingDirectory":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","isWorktree":false,"isGitRepo":true,"additionalWorkingDirectories":["/home/diogenes/.t3/userdata/attachments"],"platform":"linux","shell":"bash","osVersion":"Linux 6.19.14-108.fc42.x86_64"},"changes":[{"field":"workingDirectory","from":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0e1aab31-229f-4eb2-b217-f200f8cced01","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:41:38.308Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n# Environment update\n - Primary working directory: /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste (was /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour)\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"0e1aab31-229f-4eb2-b217-f200f8cced01","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfztGsx4yYpwo26AobEjQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Since the French captions are coarser, I'll merge the 32 English cues into sentence-level groups matching the 8 narration scenes, writing natural French translations while keeping the existing terminology conventions like \"un persona\" and \"Studio.\"\n\nFor the \"why\" scene, I'm working through how to render the English wordplay about taste and personas into French, pairing phrases like \"25 à 34 ans\" and figuring out how to carry over the joke about nobody vs. a person having taste.\n\nFor the \"measure\" scene, I'm splitting the cues about Baste starting with a person, and I'm checking how French typography handles spacing before punctuation like colons and guillemets, so I want to grep existing files for narrow no-break space usage.\n\nFor the \"fitting\" scene, I'm translating the line about adjusting an interface to a person and reworking \"same screen, three people\" into natural French phrasing.\n\nFor the \"baste\" scene, I'm working through how to render \"a vision judge examines them all\" in French, considering \"un juge visuel\" or \"un modèle de vision les juge une à une.\"\n\nFor the \"fit\" scene, I'm translating the idea of keeping the best version from each region rather than a single winner, then conveying how this reveals the true range of options before anything gets locked in.\n\nFor the \"cut\" scene, I'm starting to translate what comes out ready to use — images, vector icons, loops.\n\nThen for design tokens, checking how guide.fr.json terms this concept. In the \"talk\" scene, I'm rendering \"you can ask the persona why\" and his reply in his own words about what he likes and what would feel personal — keeping \"persona\" masculine to match the guide's usage. For \"yours,\" I'm settling on \"Venez avec vos propres personnes\" for \"bring your own people.\"\n\nI settle on \"Amenez vos propres personnes\" and continue with \"Prenez leurs mesures dans le Studio, et taillez quelque chose qui leur va\" for the next line. I also need to figure out whether the guide page requires a transcript built from the narration, likely stored as a JSON file with bilingual transcript paragraphs per chapter and duration metadata. For the media plan, I'm thinking through re-encoding the tour video from its 1920×1080 50MB render down to something web-friendly using H.264 with CRF around 22-24, faststart enabled, expecting the mostly static UI content to compress to roughly 10-15MB.\n\nSkipping a 720p variant since one 1080p file with faststart should suffice, targeting ≤15 MB with AAC audio at 160k. For the poster image, I'm weighing a few candidate frames — the end card, the \"21 drafts for one person\" method scene, or the \"Moss, measured.\" measure scene — and leaning toward the measure frame since it's distinctive, on-brand, and feels most like a designer app.\n\nFor the actual poster export, I need to pull a 1920×1080 frame and encode it as webp or JPEG, checking whether ffmpeg's libwebp encoder is available since the existing guide uses webp posters. I also need to produce bilingual caption files and short muted looping chapter clips (4–8s, downscaled H.264, no audio, faststart) from the CFR footage at sizes matching the guide's 16:10 layout — starting with a \"fitting\" clip re-cut from roughly 3.62s to 14s.\n\nBut I realize the fitting footage was recorded on the landing page's fitting room rather than the Studio's actual Fitting tab, so using it for that chapter could be misleading — I need to check the chapter text to confirm whether it's really about the Studio tab before deciding where this clip belongs. I'll go through guide.json's paragraphs for each relevant chapter (orientation, conversation, fitting, new-persona, tokens, generate) to match clips correctly — the conversation chapter's talk.mp4 clearly fits the landing page's \"Meet\" section, so I continue checking new-persona next.\n\nI'm confirming yours.mp4 matches \"Create a persona,\" tokens.mp4 matches \"Export design tokens,\" and archive.mp4 fits \"Draft prompts and generate\" since it's a dry-run replay of a recorded fal run — I should caption that honestly as a replay rather than a live run. The fitting chapter's clip choice still needs settling, and method.mp4 has no matching guide chapter so I'll skip it. For the landing page's TourSection, I'm leaning toward a narrated, click-to-play video with a poster and default captions rather than autoplay, paired with left-column copy describing a fitting walkthrough.\n\nFor layout, I want clickable chapter markers that seek the video to specific timestamps (Measure, Fitting room, Baste, Fit, Cut, Talk, Yours), framed in a stitched-border \"stage\" consistent with the site's visual style. I'm deciding to mirror the meet-intro pattern — a header row with heading and paragraph, then the full-width video, then a chapter strip of seven clickable markers below it.\n\nFor implementation, I'll use a signal to reference the video element, with chapter buttons that set currentTime and play on click, plus a timeupdate handler to track and highlight the active chapter using aria-current=\"time\". I'm also setting preload to \"metadata\" rather than eagerly loading the full video, to keep the landing page lightweight.\n\nI should check global.css for existing cursor conventions before adding anything new, and since autoplay isn't happening, reduced-motion isn't a concern here. I also want to add a \"Watch the tour\" link in the hero pointing to the tour section.\n\nRather than cramming a third CTA next to \"Meet a persona\" and \"Start your own fitting,\" I'm thinking a subtler tertiary link with a play glyph, like \"▶ Watch the 1-minute tour,\" would fit better without cluttering the hero—I'll need to read through hero.tsx fully to figure out the right placement. I also want to make the tour recording the default in the studio guide's recordings group.\n\nLooking at the existing recordings (Current Studio 0:29, Narrated tour in English and French), I'll promote the new 1:14 tour to first position with labels like \"Baste tour\" / \"La visite de Baste,\" noting it has English narration with bilingual captions, recorded October 11, 2026. I also want to show the transcript by chapter, with French captions displayed when the UI is in French.\n\nI'm adding a key prop to the video element so it re-mounts on recording or language change, and setting up a clips map linking each chapter to its clip file and caption. I'm weighing whether autoplay muted looping video inside closed `<details>` elements will still load and play given browsers typically don't render hidden content inside collapsed details.\n\nI'm leaning toward skipping the autoplay attribute entirely, using `preload=\"none\"`, and instead using an IntersectionObserver via `useVisibleTask$` to play videos only when visible and pause them otherwise, while also respecting `prefers-reduced-motion` by falling back to a controls-based player rather than autoplay.\n\nI'm sketching a reusable `LoopClip` component that handles this visibility-driven play/pause logic plus a poster frame fallback, and noting that Qwik's `useVisibleTask$` conveniently only activates when the element scrolls into view — meaning clips hidden inside closed `<details>` elements won't even run their JS until the section is expanded.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the rest of the implementation: applying the same visibility tracking to the landing page's TourSection, then verifying exact CLI flags in src/cli.ts (`--provider fal`, `--image-provider`, etc.) and checking FAL_KEY usage in `.env.example`. I also need to update README.md and docs/development.md with a \"Tour video\" section and fal provider notes, and add a `.gitignore` entry for heavy tour video assets.\n\nI'm uncertain whether site/public/media's mp4s are actually tracked in git — the ls-files output came back empty, so I should run `git status --short site/public/media` to confirm whether those files are untracked before deciding on the ignore rules, and also check the hero file and cursor conventions.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":98300,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"output_tokens":6360,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6013},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":98300,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6360,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"cache_creation_input_tokens":98300,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":98300},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":61475,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"05c18a00-043b-4104-ba3f-59328898fff8","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:42:43.102Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
