dpoint.\nsrc/evaluation/fal-judge.ts:35:  const result = await falRun<{ output?: string; error?: string | null }>(options.imageUrl ? \"fal-ai/any-llm/vision\" : \"fal-ai/any-llm\", {\nsrc/evaluation/judge.ts:123:4. **coherence** (0-1): Do all elements work together? Is the style consistent? Does it feel like one unified vision rather than random elements mashed together?\n30:    if (process.argv.includes('--voice-from-skate') && !process.env.FAL_KEY) {\n31:      process.env.FAL_KEY = execFileSync('rtk', ['proxy', 'skate', 'get', 'fal_api_key@secrets'], { encoding: 'utf8', stdio: ['ignore', 'pipe', 'pipe'] }).trim();","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"023fedba-d9a8-4410-917c-593122a1eabd","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"38c90d45-8113-4627-9d71-8e543ab48545","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01UungMsHDCCiScaipPQf9mB","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3c414e1e-d499-45e4-8da9-b06a2e9a364e","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:45:46.103Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"3c414e1e-d499-45e4-8da9-b06a2e9a364e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfztWjC6xqXpaDaPEAjjH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I need to encode the web media for the site. I'm planning to re-encode the tour video at a lower bitrate with H.264 and faststart flags, targeting around 15-20MB instead of the current 50MB render, while considering whether a separate 720p mobile version is needed.\n\nFor the poster image, I'm weighing which frame best represents the tour — the end card, the fitting room moment, or the spread showing \"eight kept, from cool to warm\" — leaning toward extracting the richest-looking frame around 43 seconds as a webp poster.\n\nI also need captions files for English and French, and I'm considering short muted chapter clips for the Studio guide. I'm trying to figure out whether the fitting chapter in the Studio guide actually shares the same FittingRoom component as the landing page demo, since the grep results weren't conclusive and I don't want to mislabel the clip if they're different.\n\nFor the other chapters, the generate and tokens clips come straight from real Studio recordings, so those are safe to use directly. The conversation chapter is trickier though, since it's recorded from the landing page's Conversation component, and I need to confirm it's the same one used in the Studio before treating it as representative.\n\nFor encoding, I'm planning on muted H.264 mp4 loops around 8-12 seconds, sourced at 1440×900 with CRF around 26-28, no audio, faststart enabled, and figuring out trim points for each clip like the archive run starting around 10.32s and finishing at 29.32s.\n\nThe archive filling section is 19 seconds, too long for a loop, so I'll speed it up roughly 2x to get near 9 seconds. I'm weighing whether to combine it with the cut section around 31-35s, but ultimately what matters most is showing the core workflow — provider selection and the dry run — since that's what's useful for someone reading the generate chapter of the guide.\n\nRight, demo mode blocks the API calls so the Studio shows the \"Demo in-browser\" badge instead of hitting real endpoints. I'm checking timing for each remaining clip: tokens runs about 8.6s at 1x, talk around 13s (maybe trim typing-wait slightly), yours about 12s at 1x or 9.7s sped up ×1.25, and fitting still needs its end point marked.\n\nI need to make sure every clip starts at 3.62s or later to avoid the dev overlay hint showing up. The method-page contact sheet take is separate from the Studio guide and isn't needed here.\n\nNext I want to check guide.json for the chapter structure — orientation, conversation, fitting, new-persona, tokens, generate — along with the French titles. Then for the landing page, I'm picturing a TourSection placed right after the hero, before Meet: a well-framed video with a short heading and a chapter list (01 Measure through 07 Yours) that seeks the video and highlights the active chapter as it plays, which would be a nice, useful touch.\n\nI'm roughing out the timestamps for each chapter — trying to decide whether the cold-open intro counts as part of 01 Measure or its own \"00 Why\" marker, then settling on approximate seek times: Measure ~0:09, Fitting room ~0:19, Baste ~0:27, Fit ~0:37, Cut ~0:45.\n\nChecking against the actual timing.json values and the visual scene transitions, I'm nudging each timestamp slightly past the cut point so clicking a chapter lands cleanly inside that scene rather than right on the transition.\n\nNow I'm drafting the copy for this section—a short, restrained heading and subtitle built around the tailoring metaphor, keeping the tone aligned with the brand's Bodoni display voice.\n\nI'm setting up the video element itself: pointing it at the tour mp4, adding a poster image, and including an English captions track with `default` set so it shows automatically, matching the earlier preference for default-on captions.\n\nSince the browser's default caption box might clash with the stage design, I'm styling `::cue` to give captions a custom background and color that fits the designed frame better. I'm also considering a custom play-button overlay on top of the poster for a more polished start experience.\n\nI want native controls to remain the reliable default, but adding a large \"Play the tour · 1:14\" button that sits over the poster and hides itself once clicked, so the experience still works without JS while feeling custom when it's active. The tricky part is making sure this overlay doesn't block the native controls once the video starts playing.\n\nClicking should start the narrated video unmuted, and chapter links should jump currentTime and resume playback while hiding the overlay. I also want timeupdate tracking to highlight the active chapter, plus a collapsible transcript section with the narration text for accessibility.\n\nFor placement, I'm thinking of inserting the tour link in the hero area, near the \"Meet a persona\" and \"Start your own fitting\" CTAs — maybe a small secondary text link with a play icon reading \"Watch the tour · 1:14\" rather than a bulky third button, since three equal CTAs would clutter the hero.\n\nOn the Studio guide page, I should also consider making the new 1:14 tour recording the default option instead of the current 0:29 clip, since it's a more complete narrated overview of the whole product.\n\nI'm mindful there's already an older English/French \"Narrated tour\" pair (walkthrough-en.mp4/walkthrough-fr.mp4) showing a previous version of Studio, so I need labels that clearly distinguish the new tour from these existing ones -- possibly renaming it \"The tour · 1:14\" with French captions overlaid on the English narration. I should check the actual docs page code to see how recording buttons are currently labeled before settling on naming.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":734,"cache_read_input_tokens":193932,"output_tokens":5319,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5238},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":734,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5319,"cache_read_input_tokens":193932,"cache_creation_input_tokens":734,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":734},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":57150,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"e4af1a2b-4b7a-4b07-88d8-e494b2e1f8eb","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:45:46.103Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
