{"parentUuid":"0f54af73-3875-42de-938a-c77b369b4c2a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfzu1imrhNGArUgR7Y7kk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm deciding between two poster options for the landing page—the \"Eight kept\" archive scene or the Fitting Room re-cut screen with its dark brown Ren theme. Since the hero section already uses the FittingRoom component, I'm leaning toward showing the \"Eight kept\" archive instead to give visual variety.\n\nFor export settings, I'm encoding the tour video at 1920×1080 webp quality ~82 for the poster, and running the ffmpeg command to transcode the source into H.264 with faststart flags, aiming for a final size between 10–18 MB while preserving text clarity in the UI screens. I'm skipping a separate mobile-optimized version since a single file should suffice.\n\nFor the chapter clips, I'm planning to encode them at 1280×800, CRF 26, no audio, with faststart, targeting roughly 1–3 MB per clip. I'm working through timing and playback speed for each clip -- the conversation clip trimmed to about 12.5 seconds at normal speed, the new-persona clip at 1.25x speed for about 9.6 seconds, the tokens clip at normal speed for 8.4 seconds, and the generate clip broken into three segments with different speeds (1.25x, 3x, and 1x) to compress the progress-and-archive-fill sequence into a tighter clip.\n\nI'm checking that the dry-run toggle sequence in the demo matches the guide's written instructions, confirming it's consistent and writing an honest caption describing the recorded fal run replay showing candidates landing by colour and density before the cut. I also need to pick representative poster frames for each clip -- the cut moment for generate, an early frame for tokens, the swatches moment for conversation, and the filled state for new-persona -- and I'm thinking about whether to script the encoding step into the build process or as a standalone script.\n\nNow I'm planning out a `scripts/publish-tour.mjs` file that encodes the render into the site's media folder with faststart, grabs a poster frame via ffmpeg's webp encoder, and handles captions -- copying the English VTT and generating a French version from translated cues, deciding where that translation data should live (likely a JSON file with cue strings matching the English captions).\n\nI'm deciding to keep timing logic consolidated in build.mjs so it generates both captions.vtt and captions.fr.vtt using the same cue timestamps, throwing if cue counts mismatch. I still need to handle chapter clip exports with their own posters, and figure out how to surface duration/chapters/transcript data to the site components without importing files from outside the Vite build root.\n\nI'm leaning toward writing a small committed tour.json generated by the publish script, with chapters and transcript entries containing both English and French text grouped by scene. I also need to double check ffmpeg has webp encoding support and confirm which ffmpeg binary is being picked up given the LD_LIBRARY_PATH environment quirks.\n\nI'll draft the French captions JSON first, then update build.mjs to also emit a captions.fr.vtt file alongside the English one.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":999,"cache_read_input_tokens":216590,"output_tokens":2606,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2296},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":999,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2606,"cache_read_input_tokens":216590,"cache_creation_input_tokens":999,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":999},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":25250,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7585be47-b023-46a8-b8f0-0d609e929066","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:51:47.590Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"7585be47-b023-46a8-b8f0-0d609e929066","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfzu1imrhNGArUgR7Y7kk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm using the \"Eight kept, from cool to warm\" frame (43 s) as the poster. Next: French subtitles (the guide is bilingual) and a reproducible publish script."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":999,"cache_read_input_tokens":216590,"output_tokens":2606,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2296},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":999,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2606,"cache_read_input_tokens":216590,"cache_creation_input_tokens":999,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":999},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8e4a13cb-2a68-4802-8c58-fbee1f0c714f","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:51:47.599Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
