{"parentUuid":"d091493b-def9-41b2-acb9-9666c638f854","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01Gm3gfbcG73F8V7G4tpcteu","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1d7291ed-bf75-4d84-86e2-14612b8195f7","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:53:07.169Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"1d7291ed-bf75-4d84-86e2-14612b8195f7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfzu5Exe8roer67QYGwE6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm thinking about French typography details, specifically whether to use non-breaking spaces inside guillemets like « les 25 à 34 ans », since the existing French guide just uses plain spaces before punctuation like colons and semicolons, and in subtitle cues narrow screens could cause awkward line breaks.\n\nI decide to keep plain spaces consistent with the existing French content since the subtitle cues are short enough not to wrap. Now I'm planning the publish script that will encode the final render to H.264/AAC MP4, generate a WebP poster frame, and handle other media processing steps for the baste-tour video.\n\nNext I'm working out how to cut short chapter clips from the raw footage for looping background use — muted, low-res H.264 with no audio, each needing to be at least 3.6 seconds and ideally 12-15 seconds total, so I'm figuring out which timestamp ranges to pull and whether to speed up portions to fit a natural excerpt length.\n\nLet me simplify the plan instead: break the clip into three ranges — 8.0→10.4 at 1× for the Generate click, 10.4→29.4 sped up ×3 through the processing, then 29.4→34.0 back at 1× for the final cut, totaling around 13.3 seconds, built with ffmpeg trim, setpts, and concat.\n\nI notice the chapter text says to leave Dry run enabled, but the recording actually shows Dry run getting unchecked right before the user clicks the button that triggers \"Getting...\" — meaning the demo replays a recorded run rather than simulating one as the guide claims. The copy seems slightly out of sync with what Studio actually does now.\n\nSo I should fix the figcaption to say something like \"Recorded in the browser demo: a real fal run for the Cyberbotanist replays, so no provider is called,\" and update the guide's generate chapter paragraph to reflect that base personas replay a recorded run while custom personas only draft prompts. This needs updating in both EN and FR copies, matching what demo-client actually does.\n\nNow I'm scanning other demo scenarios — token streaming across CSS frameworks, a persona conversation flow about colour choices, new-persona creation timing, and the landing page's fitting room distinct from the Studio's Fitting tab — to see what else in the guide needs correcting.\n\nThe orientation chapters should stick with current Studio screenshots rather than the landing-page fitting room, since mixing them would mislead users, and the method/contact-sheet page isn't a Studio feature either, so I'm narrowing down to four chapter clips: generate, tokens, conversation, and new-persona, with conversation being a nice addition since it currently lacks any screen. Now I'm thinking through clip encoding settings, likely downscaling from 1440x900 to something smaller for web delivery to keep file sizes reasonable.\n\nFor encoding I'm settling on CRF 23, slow preset, faststart flag, no audio, yuv420p pixel format, high profile at level 4.0, plus generating a WebP poster from the first frame for the poster attribute and reduced-motion fallback. For accessibility, I need to make sure autoplaying loops respect `prefers-reduced-motion`, so I'm planning a client-side hook that checks the media query and only plays the video when in view and motion is allowed, pausing when out of view to save CPU — and since most chapters are closed `<details>` by default, I need to handle videos inside those collapsed sections too.\n\nIn Qwik, I'll use `useVisibleTask$` on a `ChapterClip` component so the task only fires once the content becomes visible (which naturally happens when a closed `<details>` is opened), then wire up an IntersectionObserver to play/pause the clip. Since WCAG 2.2.2 requires a pause mechanism for auto-playing moving content, I'm leaning toward a compact custom \"Pause\"/\"Play\" toggle button in the caption row rather than heavy native controls on a muted loop.\n\nNow for the landing page tour section — I want to insert a new TourSection between Hero and Meet titled \"See it work, start to finish,\" featuring the full video with controls, poster, and bilingual caption tracks (EN default), paired with a chapter list showing timestamps that seek and play the video when clicked, plus a transcript tucked into a details element. I'm also planning to add a link from the hero into this new section.\n\nI need to pin down the exact chapter seek times by cross-referencing the rail's scene markers against the voiceover start times from timing.json, adjusting slightly earlier so each chapter click lands right before the narration begins for measure, fitting, baste, fit, cut, talk, and yours.\n\nFor the video file itself, I'm weighing resolution tradeoffs — 1920x1080 gives crisp rail text but bloats file size, while 1600x900 shaves it down but risks legibility since the rail's monospace text is already tiny at full res; given the site displays the video at under 1240px wide anyway, the lower resolution should still read fine except in fullscreen.\n\nI'm settling on 1080p with CRF 23 and a slow preset since there's real motion in the capture, then I'll need poster images, VTT caption files for EN/FR, and separate short clips for generate/tokens/conversation/new-persona sections, each with their own poster.\n\nFor the studio guide, I'm adding \"tour\" as a new recording option alongside current/en/fr, making it the default — captions will follow the page language while narration stays in English, and I'm drafting the recording note label for it.\n\nNow I'm figuring out the transcript data: rather than hand-writing it, I want to generate a tour.json file with chapters and EN/FR transcript paragraphs by grouping French caption cues against scene timing boundaries, keeping everything reproducible from source data.\n\nWriting the publish script...\n\nFor the chapter titles, I'm mapping each scene name to its French equivalent — Measure → Mesurer, Baste → Bâtir (a nice match since bâtir is the actual French couture term for basting), Fit → Ajuster, Cut → Couper, Talk → Parler — while I puzzle over whether \"Fitting room\" should be called \"Essayage\" in the guide.\n\nI'm noting that the FR guide keeps UI labels like \"Measure\" and \"Fitting\" in English since those interface elements aren't translated, but chapter titles for the video itself can be fully translated to Mesurer, Essayage, Bâtir, Ajuster, Couper, Parler, À vous. Now I need to group the French transcript cues by scene using their start times against the scene boundaries.\n\nFor chapter seek points, I'm pulling scene start times from timing.json, but noticing visual transitions sometimes occur slightly before the official scene start (e.g. fitting's scene starts at 19.267 but the visual rail begins at 18.85), so I should seek to the earlier of the two values for each chapter.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":117906,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"output_tokens":5777,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5481},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":117906,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5777,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"cache_creation_input_tokens":117906,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":117906},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":56612,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d04a61d9-2ecf-4c96-8f41-f848fc4ca368","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20