{"parentUuid":"d7c0b84b-1026-48da-a815-4bf4da9910ea","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfzu9ikLsThR6d58TeNjM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Comparing against existing walkthroughs at ~9MB for 1:53, I'm aiming for my 1:14 tour at 1080p to land around 10-14MB, so I'm drafting the publish script and testing encode sizes while working out the source clip timestamps for each chapter segment.\n\nFor the generate chapter, I trace the cursor action: starting at 8.0 with Dry run checked, unchecking it, clicking Generate around 10.3, then showing the final cut with the \"Recorded run replayed\" toast around 29.4-34.6. I settle on output as 1280x800, CRF 25, slow preset, 30fps, no audio, with faststart enabled, and decide poster frames should show the end state rather than the empty initial frame since reduced-motion users only see the poster.\n\nI then work out the actual encode command for the tour video using libx264 with CRF 22, high profile, and AAC audio, estimating the output size will shrink from 50MB to roughly 15MB. For the poster image, I'm extracting a frame at 43 seconds and converting it to WebP at 1600x900.\n\nWriting tour config JSON...\n\nFor clips, I decide the JSON should only hold src/poster/duration data while actual caption text lives in the TSX components via the translation function, and I settle on placing tour.json in the docs components folder so both the docs page and landing page can import it.\n\nNow I'm turning to the publish script, thinking through how ffmpeg needs to be invoked with execFileSync and recalling earlier issues with LD_LIBRARY_PATH needing to be unset for ffmpeg to run correctly.\n\nI'm sketching the publish-tour script that reads the HyperFrames render, captions, narration timing, and CFR takes, then writes the web encode, poster, captions, and chapter clips into the site's media and content directories.\n\nStill writing build script...\n\nStill extracting poster and captions...\n\nNow I'm pulling silent excerpts from the raw takes for the Studio guide chapters, cutting at full size rather than from the finished film so the Studio interface stays legible.\n\nWriting ffmpeg trim/concat filters...\n\nNow I need to load the narration timing data and parse the French VTT captions, grouping caption cues by scene based on their start times falling within each scene's duration window. I'm also working out the chapter title mapping, weighing whether to include the intro section alongside the seven numbered chapters in the rail navigation.\n\nI'll settle on short titles with timestamps for each chapter: Why (0:00), Measure (0:08), Fitting room (0:19), Baste (0:27), Fit (0:37), Cut (0:45), Talk (0:55), Yours (1:03), each with French equivalents too. I'm also wondering if I should pull one-line descriptions for the landing list from the rail text in the build script.\n\nI want to grab the exact chapter description copy from build.mjs so the wording stays consistent — things like \"The same screen, re-cut for three people\" for Fitting room, \"Loose drafts across the grid, each one judged\" for Baste, and similar lines for Fit, Cut, Talk, and Yours, plus their French translations. I also need to figure out seek start timing by backing off 0.3s from each scene's start (except Why, which starts at 0), and decide how to source the transcript text in English versus grouped French cues. Now I'm turning to how the landing TourSection itself should be designed to match the site's overall paper-and-ink aesthetic.\n\nFor the layout, I'm sketching desktop as a label, display headline, intro paragraph, then a video spanning most of the width alongside a clickable chapter list (time, title, description) that seeks the video, with a transcript disclosure below. On mobile it stacks and the chapters collapse into a compact grid. I'm weighing headline options that keep the tailoring metaphor, leaning toward something like \"One person, measured to the finished cut.\"\n\nI settle on the headline \"From first measurement to final cut\" with the label \"The tour · 1:14 · narrated.\" For the chapter interaction, clicking a chapter button seeks the video to its start time and plays it, while a timeupdate listener tracks playback progress to highlight the currently active chapter via aria-current — I'm working out how Qwik's event binding syntax maps JSX props like onTimeUpdate$ to the underlying native \"timeupdate\" event.\n\nI'm also second-guessing whether qwikloader's event delegation, which listens at the document level, will actually catch media events like timeupdate since those don't bubble — recalling that qwikloader may register listeners with capture:true specifically to handle non-bubbling events like focus and media events.\n\nTo be safe, I'll avoid relying on that uncertainty and instead wire up the timeupdate listener and IntersectionObserver manually inside useVisibleTask$ with a ref, since this pattern is already used elsewhere in the codebase.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6094,"cache_read_input_tokens":210524,"output_tokens":5793,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5543},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6094,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5793,"cache_read_input_tokens":210524,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6094,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6094},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":51693,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5c11f512-607b-467d-89b0-49a2602cebef","t