{"parentUuid":"d8cab8d7-ece7-46f6-abe6-a678576f43b4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_014fbSRDsDXJAocwoWBMBb64","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"70dfba87-0e40-4127-bb52-e56cceb44cb0","timestamp":"2026-10-13T20:55:31.745Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/site","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"70dfba87-0e40-4127-bb52-e56cceb44cb0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzuEzq84QBTVyEy4PcL7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm now planning the publish pipeline script that will transcode the rendered tour video into a smaller, web-optimized H.264 file with faststart, considering resolution and compression settings for a good size-quality tradeoff.\n\nI also need to produce a poster image at 43s, copy over the English and French caption files, and generate the muted looping chapter clips (archive, tokens, talk, yours, fitting) with their own posters, scaled appropriately and compressed without audio.\n\nLooking at clip timing, I'm checking the fitting take (3.62–14.04s) but realize it's from the landing page's hero FittingRoom component, not the Studio's actual Fitting tab — using it for the guide's \"Read the fitting\" chapter would be misleading, so I should skip that clip and focus on the orientation chapter instead.\n\nFor the generate/archive sequence, I'm mapping out the range showing provider selection, Dry run toggle, Generate click, progress, and the final \"The cut · 5 assets\" results — roughly 4.3 to 35.0 seconds at real-time speed, which is long but captures the full flow end to end.\n\nI'm now double-checking whether the clip actually matches the guide text, since the recording shows Dry run unchecked and a \"Recorded run replayed\" toast, while the guide describes Dry run enabled and simulated jobs — that discrepancy needs resolving before I finalize the cut.\n\nFor the tokens clip, I'm settling on 3.7 → 12.1 seconds to cover the switch from CSS variables to Tailwind to Panda and back, giving an 8.4 s segment. For the conversation clip, I'm marking the start around 3.25–3.7 s with Moss selected, then the click to Ren around 4–5 s leading into the \"What are you into?\" and \"Why these colours?\" exchange.\n\nChecking the talk take's end mark against the recorded cut, I'll settle on 3.7 → 16.9 for a clean ~17 s clip, and note this scene matches the landing page conversation chapter about meeting Moss, Ren, and Ada.\n\nFor new-persona, I'm using the 3.54 s start where \"The Night Potter\" name and description get typed, trimming to 3.7 → 16.4 for a 16.5 s clip. So that's four clips total — generate, tokens, conversation, new-persona — and now I'm picking poster frame timestamps for each: the cut point at 34.5 for generate, the Tailwind moment at 5 for tokens, the palette swatches at 16.2 for conversation, and still working out the frame for new-persona.\n\nNow I'm weighing whether chapter clips should autoplay. Since the guide's chapters are collapsible `<details>` elements with only 'orientation' open by default, I want a pattern where clips are still until requested, respecting prefers-reduced-motion and WCAG's rule that auto-playing content over 5 seconds needs a pause control. I'm leaning toward reusing the MotionStudy pattern — a poster still with a \"Watch it\" play/pause button — rather than a more polished but riskier autoplay-on-open approach.\n\nFollowing the codebase's existing idiom, I'll build a small `GuideClip` component mirroring MotionStudy's click-to-play pattern, placed in the docs components folder and styled via guide.css with bilingual label props. For placement, I'm identifying which chapters (conversation, new-persona, tokens, generate) currently show outdated or missing stills, and planning to swap their figures for clips with appropriate captions.\n\nI need to check the footage file timestamps to get an accurate recording date for the caption. Then for the landing page TourSection, I'm thinking through section copy that matches the house voice established by the hero (\"Cut to fit one person\") and Meet section — something like \"Seventy-four seconds, start to finish\" as a heading for the tour placed right after the hero.\n\nFor the copy itself, I'll go with \"See Baste work.\" as the heading, paired with a short paragraph describing the narrated tour covering measuring, cutting, the archive, and the conversation with Ren. I want clickable chapter chips (01 Measure, 02 Fitting room, 03 Baste, 04 Fit, 05 Cut, 06 Talk, 07 Yours) that seek the video to specific timestamps, which adds a nice functional/designer touch since they'll inherit the cursor pin styling automatically as buttons. Now I'm setting up the video element with controls, metadata preload, and a poster image.\n\nI'm adding English and French caption tracks, defaulting captions on since this is accessible and also helps for muted viewing, even though native caption rendering might slightly overlap the video's lower area — that's acceptable. I don't want autoplay since it's narrated; instead I'm considering a styled overlay play button on top of the poster that reads something like \"Play the tour · 1:14,\" which calls play() and then hides itself so native controls take over afterward.\n\nI'm wiring up chapter buttons that seek the video to a given timestamp and start playback, and using the timeupdate event to track which chapter is currently active so I can highlight it with aria-current. For styling, I'll follow the existing pattern of global CSS classes used for the \"meet\" section and add similar styles for this new tour section nearby in the global stylesheet.\n\nNow I'm thinking through the hero CTAs — currently there's a primary dark button for \"Meet a persona\" and a text link for \"Start your own fitting.\" Adding a third link for the tour video feels cluttered with three CTAs, so I'm weighing whether the tour link should actually replace or reorder the primary CTA since the tour section immediately follows the hero.\n\nI'll keep it simple: a text link \"Watch the 1-minute tour\" alongside the existing button and \"Start your own fitting\" link, since a flex-wrap row with one button and two text links reads fine. I don't think I need to add \"Tour\" to the nav alongside personas, method, pattern book, materials, and studio guide. For the studio guide recordings, I'm adding a \"Product tour · 1:14\" option with English narration and French captions, and considering whether it should become the new default recording instead of \"Current.\"\n\nI'm structuring the tour data as a JSON file with file, poster, duration, chapters (bilingual titles with timestamps), and transcript entries joining the French and English cue lines per scene, so the landing section can reuse the same chapter data. I'm also noting the chapter rail naming convention in the video, like \"01 Measure.\"\n\nLooking at the seek timestamps, I want to align each chapter marker with the visual wipe transitions rather than the raw cue times -- so Measure seeks to roughly 8.6s, Fitting room to 18.85s, Baste to 26.85s, Fit to 36.7s, Cut to 44.95s, and similarly for Talk and Yours based on their transition starts.\n\nI'm also deciding whether to include \"Why\" as an opening chapter at 0:00 to match the video's own 7-item index, keeping the site's chapter list consistent with the rail navigation rather than adding or omitting entries. For French localization, I'm mapping names like Mesurer, Cabine d'essayage, and considering Bâtir or Faufiler for \"Baste\" since that's the proper sewing term in French.\n\nI'm now working through remaining items: translating the rest of the chapter titles to French (Ajuster, Couper, Parler, À vous), deciding to keep \"Baste\" as the product name since it refers to the tool itself, then moving on to the developer docs — I need to read the full developers page to properly add a fal provider entry and a tour video section, update the README and development docs with tour info, and figure out what should go in .gitignore for the heavy video asset directories like footage, renders, and snapshots.\n\nI'm thinking through which large regenerable directories to exclude from git — renders, snapshots, .work, footage-v1, and the raw bed-source music file — while being careful about footage/*.webm since those raw recordings feed into the build script and may need different handling depending on size. I also want to check the size of the old footage-v1 take set before deciding whether to delete it, since it's an earlier artifact of my own recording work.\n\nEven though deleting 160 MB of superseded recordings isn't really harmful, I'd rather be cautious and move it to a cache directory instead, something reversible rather than outright deletion.\n\nNext I need to run through the test suite: type checking, linting, build, and tests for both the site and the root project. Then I should visually verify by starting the dev server and taking Playwright screenshots of the landing tour section and docs page, making sure the server runs in a detached process so restarts don't kill it.\n\nFor leaving things tidy afterward, I'm debating whether to leave the dev server running at the end given the user had started one earlier for review, or stop it -- I'll decide that later. Before writing the publish script, I should also note memory updates and check the footage dates and sizes first.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":122365,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"output_tokens":6560,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":6388},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":122365,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6560,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"cache_creation_input_tokens":122365,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":122365},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":68669,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0