{"parentUuid":"e7b72f0f-fa0a-4cf2-acfc-d7311660ba77","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_01DL38pHqFkeJrDciYUQZdPw","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"67dc6338-952b-4621-b359-d03d93892c15","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:02:01.534Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"67dc6338-952b-4621-b359-d03d93892c15","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzumCpGeGfmYxVLHpzVr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"All the publish outputs check out—18.7 MB for the 74s 1080p tour is a sensible bitrate. Now I'm working out the chapter start times from the video for the site's chapter markers, starting with where \"Measure\" begins after the intro scene ends around 8.7s.\n\nI'm mapping the full set of chapter timestamps against the video's own chapter list (01 Measure through 07 Yours), treating the \"why\" section as an intro before the formal chapters. For the landing page I want a chapter rail beside the video that seeks to each timestamp, matching the editorial feel of the video itself.\n\nI'm thinking through the TourSection design now—the user wants something designer-grade rather than \"ugly cards,\" so I'm picturing a big video framed with a stitched dashed-red seam, a strong editorial heading, a seeking chapter list on the side, and the transcript tucked into a details element. I'm checking existing landing CSS classes to keep the styling consistent with the rest of the site.\n\nNow I'm sketching the actual TourSection component: a labeled header with timing info and a descriptive subhead, followed by a video element with captions in English and French. I want a custom poster with a large play button overlay rather than the browser's default controls, so I'm planning a signal to toggle into playing state on click.\n\nI'll add chapter buttons that seek and play the video, highlighting the active chapter as it plays, plus a collapsible transcript and download/caption links in the footer. For the hero, I'll add a quieter \"Watch the tour · 1:14\" link alongside the existing CTAs, then assemble the landing page section order with HeroSection, TourSection, MeetSection, and ClosingSection in sequence.\n\nFor the Studio guide, I'm making the tour recording the new default option, labeled \"The Baste tour · 1:14,\" with English narration and French subtitles available, extending the recording type to include 'tour' alongside the existing options.\n\nBoth the landing section and guide could import this JSON. I also realize there's an aspect-ratio mismatch: the existing walkthroughs are 1440×900 (16:10) but the tour video is 16:9, so the hardcoded CSS aspect-ratio of 16/10 on `.guide-watch video` won't display correctly even with explicit width/height attributes.\n\nThe fix is to add a data attribute like `data-ratio=\"wide\"` so wide videos get their own aspect-ratio rule instead of inheriting the default. I'm also thinking through chapter clips — right now several chapters (tokens, conversation, new-persona, generate) just show static old screenshots, so I want to replace them with a `ChapterClip` component showing a poster image plus a \"Watch it move\" button that plays a muted looping clip, similar to the MotionStudy pattern.\n\nSince the chapters are collapsed `<details>` elements, videos only load when opened, so I'm leaning toward autoplaying muted loops on open rather than requiring a click, but need to respect prefers-reduced-motion and WCAG's requirement for a pause control on auto-moving content past five seconds — so I'll autoplay when the chapter is open and in view, reduced motion isn't set, and include a visible pause button.\n\nFor captions on the clips, I'm thinking something like \"Recorded in the Studio demo · October 2026\" with a French equivalent, noting the Studio UI itself stays in English even for French readers.\n\nFor the orientation/fitting chapters I'll just keep the existing current/fitting.png still as-is.\n\nFor developer docs, I need to add fal as a provider with its CLI flag and key, listing the models used per stage (Seedream v4, Recraft v3, Seedance 1 Pro, any-llm vision as judge), plus a new \"Tour video\" section documenting the full pipeline: record, narrate, score, build, check, render, publish, with the corresponding commands.\n\nI'm also planning to add a sections entry for the tour video page, mention the tour in the README near the top with a link, add a matching pipeline section to development.md covering environment caveats like LD_LIBRARY_PATH, the ldd shim, and HYPERFRAMES_RENDER_DETACHED, and figure out .gitignore rules — committing the smaller site media for deploy while excluding the large footage and render directories.\n\nSince the published copy already lives in `site/public/media/tour`, the render output is reproducible scratch, so it's safe to ignore. As for `footage-v1` (about 157 MB), it's old take material from earlier sessions—deleting it is harder to reverse, so I should be cautious before removing it outright.\n\nI'll gitignore it rather than delete it and just flag it in the report for the user, since deletion is irreversible and wasn't requested; same approach for `.work`. For testing, I need to run root `npm test`, then in site run type checking, lint, build, and tests.\n\nFor visual verification, I should spin up the dev server and capture screenshots of the tour section, guide, and docs at both desktop and mobile widths. I'll check whether Playwright is available locally or need to point to the cached module used by the recorder, or alternatively just use the T3 preview browser tools against localhost, starting the server detached with setsid/nohup so it survives restarts.\n\nI remember dev servers get restarted via `scripts/runtime.mjs` after T3 restarts, so I should check how that's invoked. I also need to save key memories, and for the final report I'll embed the contact sheet image directly using an absolute file path in markdown. On the encode quality side, CRF 22 with stillimage tuning at 18.7MB seems fine, though I should reconsider whether stillimage tuning is right given the tour has camera pans rather than being fully static.\n\nNow I want to pull up the actual hero component, the global.css styles, and the README to get the exact content I need to edit, starting with reading hero.tsx.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":126065,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"output_tokens":4838,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":4539},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":126065,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":4838,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"cache_creation_input_tokens":126065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":126065},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":48784,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"cec6c5ea-dfff-4e95-a046-8d6a40b8c388","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:02:01.534Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
