{"parentUuid":"522154cf-8cae-45c4-aee4-ab8f7482747b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzvYYwzf5bYtEuzc7rfk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Qw2eh1c3VTVE6f7S8c5jyK","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste && grep -n \"fal-ai/[a-z0-9./-]*\" -o src/assets/generators.ts src/evaluation/fal-judge.ts src/config/baste-config.ts | sort -u; echo ---; node -e \"\nconst en=require('./site/src/components/docs/guide.json');\nfor (const id of ['conversation','generate','new-persona','tokens']) { const c=en.find(x=>x.id===id); console.log('##', id, '|', c.title, '|', c.href); c.paragraphs.forEach(p=>console.log('  -', p)); }\"","description":"List fal model IDs and the four clip chapters' text"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":140196,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"output_tokens":15216,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":14880},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":140196,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":15216,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"cache_creation_input_tokens":140196,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":140196},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Qw2eh1c3VTVE6f7S8c5jyK":{"command":"cd /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste && grep -n \"fal-ai/[a-z0-9./-]*\" -o src/assets/generators.ts src/evaluation/fal-judge.ts src/config/baste-config.ts | sort -u; echo ---; node -e \"\nconst en=require('./site/src/components/docs/guide.json');\nfor (const id of ['conversation','generate','new-persona','tokens']) { const c=en.find(x=>x.id===id); console.log('##', id, '|', c.title, '|', c.href); c.paragraphs.forEach(p=>console.log('  -', p)); }\"","description":"List fal model IDs and the four clip chapters' text"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d9b8e735-3cb7-4fef-8535-170622da6821","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:13:57.794Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/site","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"d9b8e735-3cb7-4fef-8535-170622da6821","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4f5ed931-9f1d-475a-be32-8d6a81df3ec7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Qw2eh1c3VTVE6f7S8c5jyK","type":"tool_result","content":"src/assets/generators.ts:124:fal-ai/recraft/v3/text-to-image/api\nsrc/assets/generators.ts:206:fal-ai/bytedance/seedream/v4/text-to-image\nsrc/assets/generators.ts:437:fal-ai/bytedance/seedance/v1/pro/text-to-video\nsrc/assets/generators.ts:480:fal-ai/bytedance/seedance/v1/pro/text-to-video/api\nsrc/assets/generators.ts:85:fal-ai/recraft/v3/text-to-image\nsrc/evaluation/fal-judge.ts:35:fal-ai/any-llm\nsrc/evaluation/fal-judge.ts:35:fal-ai/any-llm/vision\nsrc/evaluation/fal-judge.ts:7:fal-ai/any-llm/vision/api\n---\n## conversation | Talk with a companion | /#meet\n  - Meet Moss, Ren and Ada on the home page. Each has a different cultural world and a conversation about their taste. The label tells you whether you are exploring an authored guided demo or an AI conversation.\n  - When voice is available, tap Talk and allow microphone access. Tap Finish when you are done; you can speak for up to 45 seconds. Your audio goes to fal for transcription. Review or edit the words in the message field, then press Send. Cancel discards the recording.\n  - Turn on Spoken replies to hear future answers, or choose Listen to reply for the latest one. The indicator distinguishes listening, thinking, preparing a voice, speaking and paused playback. Pause keeps your place; Resume continues; Stop ends playback. Switching companions or leaving the tab stops the microphone and audio.\n  - Typing remains available when voice is unavailable or permission is denied. The conversation keeps each companion’s messages and draft while you switch, but does not save them across a page reload.\n## generate | Draft prompts and generate | /gui/?tab=generate\n  - Open Generate and leave Dry run enabled for your first attempt. Choose Asset suite or Full UI kit, then Draft the prompts. Read the image, SVG and video briefs before making images.\n  - In the browser demo, jobs are simulated and no assets are generated. With generation available, choose an image model and review your spending limit before turning off Dry run. Follow the job’s progress and reopen earlier jobs from the history.\n  - Hosted generation covers images and judging. A full kit also needs SVG and video services. If a service is unavailable, you can still draft prompts and continue refining your persona.\n## new-persona | Create a persona | /gui/?new=1\n  - Choose New persona. Enter a name, check its generated slug, add a region and a short description. The slug is a lowercase identifier used in routes and file names; it is separate from the display name.\n  - Fill Culture with subcultures and values. In Influences, list films, anime or shows, music genres, musicians and visual artists. Habitat covers spaces, tools and obsessions. Behaviour captures software values and pet peeves. Separate list items with commas.\n  - In The cut, choose the aesthetic axes, then add visual and mood keywords. Be concrete: a named film, a familiar place and an actual working habit give a clearer brief than a generic adjective. The completion meter counts filled measurements; it is not a quality score.\n  - Select Add to wardrobe. A successful save selects the new persona and returns to Fitting. A name is required. Keep a unique slug to avoid replacing another custom persona. Cancel returns without saving the form.\n## tokens | Export design tokens | /gui/?tab=tokens\n  - Open Tokens and choose CSS variables, Tailwind, Panda or JSON. The code panel updates for the selected format. CSS produces .css, Tailwind .js, Panda .ts and JSON .json.\n  - Copy sends the displayed export to the browser clipboard. Download saves a file named after the persona. If clipboard access is denied, use Download or select the code manually. The code and variable identifiers stay unchanged when the UI language changes.\n  - The side panels show the spacing scale, radius and shadow samples, and easing curves. Hover an easing row to preview motion. These are integration references, not an automatic installation into your app.\n  - Downloads survive a demo reset because they are browser files. In the demo, saving an OpenPencil document does not regenerate these exports; export tokens and the editable document are separate demo stores.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"146ae1e4-ca8d-4161-a78f-421566f89df3","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:13:57.875Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"src/assets/generators.ts:124:fal-ai/recraft/v3/text-to-image/api\nsrc/assets/generators.ts:206:fal-ai/bytedance/seedream/v4/text-to-image\nsrc/assets/generators.ts:437:fal-ai/bytedance/seedance/v1/pro/text-to-video\nsrc/assets/generators.ts:480:fal-ai/bytedance/seedance/v1/pro/text-to-video/api\nsrc/assets/generators.ts:85:fal-ai/recraft/v3/text-to-image\nsrc/evaluation/fal-judge.ts:35:fal-ai/any-llm\nsrc/evaluation/fal-judge.ts:35:fal-ai/any-llm/vision\nsrc/evaluation/fal-judge.ts:7:fal-ai/any-llm/vision/api\n---\n## conversation | Talk with a companion | /#meet\n  - Meet Moss, Ren and Ada on the home page. Each has a different cultural world and a conversation about their taste. The label tells you whether you are exploring an authored guided demo or an AI conversation.\n  - When voice is available, tap Talk and allow microphone access. Tap Finish when you are done; you can speak for up to 45 seconds. Your audio goes to fal for transcription. Review or edit the words in the message field, then press Send. Cancel discards the recording.\n  - Turn on Spoken replies to hear future answers, or choose Listen to reply for the latest one. The indicator distinguishes listening, thinking, preparing a voice, speaking and paused playback. Pause keeps your place; Resume continues; Stop ends playback. Switching companions or leaving the tab stops the microphone and audio.\n  - Typing remains available when voice is unavailable or permission is denied. The conversation keeps each companion’s messages and draft while you switch, but does not save them across a page reload.\n## generate | Draft prompts and generate | /gui/?tab=generate\n  - Open Generate and leave Dry run enabled for your first attempt. Choose Asset suite or Full UI kit, then Draft the prompts. Read the image, SVG and video briefs before making images.\n  - In the browser demo, jobs are simulated and no assets are generated. With generation available, choose an image model and review your spending limit before turning off Dry run. Follow the job’s progress and reopen earlier jobs from the history.\n  - Hosted generation covers images and judging. A full kit also needs SVG and video services. If a service is unavailable, you can still draft prompts and continue refining your persona.\n## new-persona | Create a persona | /gui/?new=1\n  - Choose New persona. Enter a name, check its generated slug, add a region and a short description. The slug is a lowercase identifier used in routes and file names; it is separate from the display name.\n  - Fill Culture with subcultures and values. In Influences, list films, anime or shows, music genres, musicians and visual artists. Habitat covers spaces, tools and obsessions. Behaviour captures software values and pet peeves. Separate list items with commas.\n  - In The cut, choose the aesthetic axes, then add visual and mood keywords. Be concrete: a named film, a familiar place and an actual working habit give a clearer brief than a generic adjective. The completion meter counts filled measurements; it is not a quality score.\n  - Select Add to wardrobe. A successful save selects the new persona and returns to Fitting. A name is required. Keep a unique slug to avoid replacing another custom persona. Cancel returns without saving the form.\n## tokens | Export design tokens | /gui/?tab=tokens\n  - Open Tokens and choose CSS variables, Tailwind, Panda or JSON. The code panel updates for the selected format. CSS produces .css, Tailwind .js, Panda .ts and JSON .json.\n  - Copy sends the displayed export to the browser clipboard. Download saves a file named after the persona. If clipboard access is denied, use Download or select the code manually. The code and variable identifiers stay unchanged when the UI language changes.\n  - The side panels show the spacing scale, radius and shadow samples, and easing curves. Hover an easing row to preview motion. These are integration references, not an automatic installation into your app.\n  - Downloads survive a demo reset because they are browser files. In the demo, saving an OpenPencil document does not regenerate these exports; export tokens and the editable document are separate demo stores.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"d9b8e735-3cb7-4fef-8535-170622da6821","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
