{"parentUuid":"5770e3dd-2626-40cc-82f4-8bb7900792ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzvkzVED5itfK9NDQgaZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019pjVHyj4e75xHCQ75bmLBS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"sed -n 1,50p README.md; echo ---; grep -n \"Provider\\|provider\\|FAL\\|fal\\b\\|Environment\\|API key\\|## \" README.md | sed -n 1,60p | grep -v \"^ *#\" | head -40","description":"Read the README intro and provider sections"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4781,"cache_read_input_tokens":249561,"output_tokens":286,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4781,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":286,"cache_read_input_tokens":249561,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4781,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4781},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019pjVHyj4e75xHCQ75bmLBS":{"command":"cd /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste && sed -n 1,50p README.md; echo ---; grep -n \"Provider\\|provider\\|FAL\\|fal\\b\\|Environment\\|API key\\|## \" README.md | sed -n 1,60p | grep -v \"^ *#\" | head -40","description":"Read the README intro and provider sections"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_019pjVHyj4e75xHCQ75bmLBS":{"cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8fdfd4a6-e31c-4c83-82ba-005d197d6fcf","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:14:17.507Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"8fdfd4a6-e31c-4c83-82ba-005d197d6fcf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4f5ed931-9f1d-475a-be32-8d6a81df3ec7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019pjVHyj4e75xHCQ75bmLBS","type":"tool_result","content":"# Baste\n\n**Interfaces cut to fit one person.**\n\n![One interface, fitted to three personas](docs/fitting-loop.gif)\n\n*Baste (v.) — to tack a garment together with long, loose stitches so it can be fitted before the final cut.*\n\nBaste takes a persona's films, music, rooms, tools and obsessions, and from them drafts the design system, icons,\nimages and motion that fit. Palettes and typefaces are derived from the persona's cultural references, so no two\npersonas come out the same. Then it explores many candidates with quality-diversity search, judges them for\npersona fit, and cuts the winners into production assets.\n\nNow with **semantic version control for design systems** and **OpenPencil bridge** for editable design components.\n\n## The Studio\n\n```bash\nnpx baste gui        # local API on :3456 — then open the site's /gui route\n```\n\nThe Studio (`site/`, route `/gui`) puts one persona at the centre: see it **wearing its own design** (a live\ntry-on of the same screen in its tokens, with contrast checks), export tokens, draft prompts and generate assets\nwith a staged progress view, pin a moodboard, read a decomposed brand kit, teach it your taste, and edit tokens\nas an OpenPencil document. Without a local server it runs in demo mode on the built-in personas.\n\nStart the API and Qwik Studio together from the repository root:\n\n```bash\ndevenv tasks run baste:install\ndevenv up\n```\n\nOpen `http://localhost:5173/gui/` for the Studio and `http://localhost:5173/docs/` for documentation.\nThe site proxies `/api` to the Baste API on port 3456. Storybook is opt-in.\nSee [local development](docs/development.md) for tasks, port overrides and verification boundaries.\n\n## Not Organic accounts\n\nStudio Settings includes profile creation/sign-in through Not Organic, the authorized model catalog,\nwallet credit and advertised checkout offers. Hosted image generation and Jev judging use server-held\nPKCE/DPoP authorization. Design personas are separate from the public account profile, and account-owned\ndesign files are isolated by DID. Local CLI generation continues to use your selected provider keys.\n\nEnable `NOTORGANIC_ENABLED=true` with an exact `BASTE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN` after registering Baste's product\nand origin on the provider. Payments require provider-configured offers and an HTTPS return origin.\nSource integration does not establish that a deployed sign-in or paid checkout works.\nSee [Not Organic integration](docs/notorganic.md) for the configuration and API contract.\n\n## Quick Start\n---\n16:## The Studio\n38:## Not Organic accounts\n43:design files are isolated by DID. Local CLI generation continues to use your selected provider keys.\n46:and origin on the provider. Payments require provider-configured offers and an HTTPS return origin.\n50:## Quick Start\n60:## Commands\n62:### Browse Personas\n69:### Create Custom Personas\n84:### Generate Assets\n100:### Design Version Control\n126:### Decompose a Live Site\n156:### Remix Personas\n164:### Cultural Experiences\n181:### Export / Share / Import\n204:### Configuration\n220:### Web GUI\n229:## Configuration File\n248:    \"image\": { \"provider\": \"openai\", \"model\": \"gpt-image-2\" },\n249:    \"svg\": { \"provider\": \"quiver\" },\n250:    \"video\": { \"provider\": \"veo\" }\n255:## Programmatic API\n257:### Persona Management\n286:### Design Version Control\n334:### Semantic Change Types\n352:### OpenPencil Bridge\n373:## Built-in Personas\n381:## `.baste` File Format\n408:## Environment Variables\n418:## Architecture\n434:## License","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b20f6211-14a5-46ab-80dd-41d5d88779d7","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:14:17.540Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Baste\n\n**Interfaces cut to fit one person.**\n\n![One interface, fitted to three personas](docs/fitting-loop.gif)\n\n*Baste (v.) — to tack a garment together with long, loose stitches so it can be fitted before the final cut.*\n\nBaste takes a persona's films, music, rooms, tools and obsessions, and from them drafts the design system, icons,\nimages and motion that fit. Palettes and typefaces are derived from the persona's cultural references, so no two\npersonas come out the same. Then it explores many candidates with quality-diversity search, judges them for\npersona fit, and cuts the winners into production assets.\n\nNow with **semantic version control for design systems** and **OpenPencil bridge** for editable design components.\n\n## The Studio\n\n```bash\nnpx baste gui        # local API on :3456 — then open the site's /gui route\n```\n\nThe Studio (`site/`, route `/gui`) puts one persona at the centre: see it **wearing its own design** (a live\ntry-on of the same screen in its tokens, with contrast checks), export tokens, draft prompts and generate assets\nwith a staged progress view, pin a moodboard, read a decomposed brand kit, teach it your taste, and edit tokens\nas an OpenPencil document. Without a local server it runs in demo mode on the built-in personas.\n\nStart the API and Qwik Studio together from the repository root:\n\n```bash\ndevenv tasks run baste:install\ndevenv up\n```\n\nOpen `http://localhost:5173/gui/` for the Studio and `http://localhost:5173/docs/` for documentation.\nThe site proxies `/api` to the Baste API on port 3456. Storybook is opt-in.\nSee [local development](docs/development.md) for tasks, port overrides and verification boundaries.\n\n## Not Organic accounts\n\nStudio Settings includes profile creation/sign-in through Not Organic, the authorized model catalog,\nwallet credit and advertised checkout offers. Hosted image generation and Jev judging use server-held\nPKCE/DPoP authorization. Design personas are separate from the public account profile, and account-owned\ndesign files are isolated by DID. Local CLI generation continues to use your selected provider keys.\n\nEnable `NOTORGANIC_ENABLED=true` with an exact `BASTE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN` after registering Baste's product\nand origin on the provider. Payments require provider-configured offers and an HTTPS return origin.\nSource integration does not establish that a deployed sign-in or paid checkout works.\nSee [Not Organic integration](docs/notorganic.md) for the configuration and API contract.\n\n## Quick Start\n---\n16:## The Studio\n38:## Not Organic accounts\n43:design files are isolated by DID. Local CLI generation continues to use your selected provider keys.\n46:and origin on the provider. Payments require provider-configured offers and an HTTPS return origin.\n50:## Quick Start\n60:## Commands\n62:### Browse Personas\n69:### Create Custom Personas\n84:### Generate Assets\n100:### Design Version Control\n126:### Decompose a Live Site\n156:### Remix Personas\n164:### Cultural Experiences\n181:### Export / Share / Import\n204:### Configuration\n220:### Web GUI\n229:## Configuration File\n248:    \"image\": { \"provider\": \"openai\", \"model\": \"gpt-image-2\" },\n249:    \"svg\": { \"provider\": \"quiver\" },\n250:    \"video\": { \"provider\": \"veo\" }\n255:## Programmatic API\n257:### Persona Management\n286:### Design Version Control\n334:### Semantic Change Types\n352:### OpenPencil Bridge\n373:## Built-in Personas\n381:## `.baste` File Format\n408:## Environment Variables\n418:## Architecture\n434:## License","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8fdfd4a6-e31c-4c83-82ba-005d197d6fcf","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"b20f6211-14a5-46ab-80dd-41d5d88779d7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzvkzVED5itfK9NDQgaZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0158YowbkWasf3hk6P2Qpr1F","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"rtk proxy cat docs/development.md","description":"Read the development guide verbatim"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4781,"cache_read_input_tokens":249561,"output_tokens":286,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4781,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":286,"cache_read_input_tokens":249561,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4781,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4781},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0158YowbkWasf3hk6P2Qpr1F":{"command":"cd /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste && rtk proxy cat docs/development.md","description":"Read the development guide verbatim"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_0158YowbkWasf3hk6P2Qpr1F":{"cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"baa3ca72-a108-4c49-a264-cd75255633d0","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:14:18.114Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"baa3ca72-a108-4c49-a264-cd75255633d0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4f5ed931-9f1d-475a-be32-8d6a81df3ec7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0158YowbkWasf3hk6P2Qpr1F","type":"tool_result","content":"# Local development\n\nUse Nix and Devenv from the repository root. Native tasks run npm scripts with Node and install frozen dependencies using the root and site `package-lock.json` files.\n\n```sh\ndevenv shell\ndevenv tasks run baste:install\ndevenv up\n```\n\n`devenv up` starts the Baste API on port 3456 and the Qwik site on port 5173. Open `http://localhost:5173/gui/` for the Studio or `http://localhost:5173/docs/` for documentation. The site proxies `/api` to the local API, keeping session cookies on one origin.\n\nThe bundled GUI served by `baste gui` is also available on the API port. It is a local legacy interface; the Qwik Studio owns the account, wallet and live hosted-model UI.\n\nIf the running site reports a missing import for a source file that now exists, restart just the site with `devenv processes restart site`. Vite can retain an SSR import failure when the importing file is updated before the new module is created. Check the rendered Studio and browser console after recovery: a development error page can return HTTP 200, so a successful health request alone does not verify the page.\n\n## Saved projects\n\nOpen **Projects** in the Studio to give an application a brief and choose an audience persona. Projects retain their own audience snapshot, so editing a source persona does not silently alter an existing project. Each saved change creates a revision; restoring an earlier revision creates a new history entry.\n\nLocal projects are stored in `.baste/projects`. Hosted projects use the signed-in Not Organic account's directory under `.baste/accounts`. These private runtime files are ignored by Git. Concurrent changes return a conflict so the Studio can retain the draft and offer the latest saved version. Repeated requests with the same command ID do not create duplicate changes.\n\nThis is the first milestone of the [design partner plan](plans/design-partner.md). Generated characters, conversational refinement, GPT-Live and stop-motion performance are subsequent milestones.\n\nAn interrupted writer can leave a project lock behind. If a saved project keeps reporting that it is busy after a server crash, stop every Baste process using that storage before repairing the specific lock. From the same working directory as the server, after building:\n\n```sh\ndevenv processes down\nnode dist/src/projects/repair-lock.js --project <project-id> --server-stopped\n# For a hosted project, also supply its owner's DID:\nnode dist/src/projects/repair-lock.js --project <project-id> --account <owner-did> --server-stopped\ndevenv up\n```\n\nThe repair preserves project history and command receipts. It refuses a live lock owner, a changed file or a symlink. The stopped-server precondition also covers other workers or replicas sharing this directory; run the appropriate local or hosted command once, then restart. This operation is deliberately unavailable to browser and agent callers.\n\n## Tasks\n\n| Task | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| `baste:install` | Install root and site dependencies from their lockfiles |\n| `baste:api` | Start the Baste API |\n| `baste:site` | Start the Qwik site and Studio |\n| `baste:docs` | Start the site for its `/docs/` route |\n| `baste:storybook` | Start Storybook |\n| `baste:dev` | Start the configured development processes with `devenv up` |\n| `baste:build` | Build the CLI/package and site |\n| `baste:typecheck` | Check root and site TypeScript |\n| `baste:lint` | Check frontend lint rules |\n| `baste:test` | Run existing root tests |\n| `baste:check` | Run the configured validation tasks |\n| `baste:storybook:build` | Build the component explorer |\n\n```sh\ndevenv tasks list\ndevenv tasks run baste:typecheck\ndevenv tasks run baste:check\n```\n\nStorybook does not start by default. Enable its process when needed:\n\n```sh\nBASTE_WITH_STORYBOOK=1 devenv up\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\nCopy `.env.example` to `.env` and configure the providers you use. Do not commit `.env` or a config file containing private keys.\n\n- `BASTE_API_PORT`: API process port, default `3456`.\n- `BASTE_SITE_PORT`: Qwik development port, default `5173`.\n- `BASTE_STORYBOOK_PORT`: Storybook port, default `6006`.\n- `BASTE_WITH_STORYBOOK=1`: opt-in Storybook process.\n- `BASTE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN`: exact browser origin for account callbacks and CSRF checks. Devenv sets `http://localhost:5173`; the standalone API defaults to `http://localhost:3456`. Set it explicitly when running the Qwik Studio outside Devenv, changing its port or serving a deployed Studio.\n\nThe Studio uses `/api` by default. Its Settings connection field supports an explicit API URL for local development. Account mode requires the configured Studio origin and a same-origin proxy. A public static site needs its hosting layer to route `/api` to Baste; a static build alone does not provide the account API.\n\nFor local generation, configure `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `QUIVER_API_KEY`, `GOOGLE_API_KEY`, and any other selected provider's settings. Run `baste config --init` for a local `baste.config.json`. Preview prompts with `baste generate cyberbotanist --dry-run` before spending provider credit.\n\nThe public persona conversation at `/#meet` uses authored replies when no conversation model is available. In local mode, `OPENAI_API_KEY` enables open-ended replies through `POST /api/converse/:id`; `BASTE_CONVERSATION_MODEL` selects the model (default `gpt-4o`). Restart the API after changing these values. `/api/health` reports `conversation.mode` as `ai` or `demo`. Account mode always disables this local-key path. Hosted AI conversation still needs a metered account transport; the public page labels its authored demo explicitly. Failed AI replies remain visible with a retry action, and never silently become demo replies.\n\nTechnical explanations, scoring, exports and local setup are at `/method/`. The public landing page introduces the personas. Lenis and Tempus run only on the landing and Method pages; inner chat and Studio scrollers remain native. The Method page's decorative Strands composition from shaders.com loads on visibility, with a static fallback for unavailable WebGPU and reduced motion. The heading reveal adapts React Bits' BlurText treatment to Qwik without adding a React runtime.\n\nThe public conversation reuses the Moss, Ren and Ada portraits from the October 8 companion workroom studies, recovered from worktree `73bc` through the local Entire session history. Their source prompts and asset provenance are in [companion-portraits.json](companion-portraits.json). They are illustrated example characters; the page does not claim that runtime portrait generation or the full Studio partner workflow is implemented. The conversation keeps the atelier typography and writing surface stable, while palette and type samples show each persona's design choices inline.\n\nFor the hosted account path, see [Not Organic integration](notorganic.md). Local CLI calls do not receive a browser's hosted account session.\n\n## Verification boundaries\n\nThe fabric regression check exercises window resizing, a lost WebGL context, and touch viewport changes while scrolling. It checks that no resized canvas reaches paint before being redrawn, inspects the rendered background, and saves screenshots plus a report under `/tmp/baste-fabric-qa`:\n\n```sh\nrtk proxy node site/scripts/verify-fabric.mjs\n```\n\nSet `PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE` to an installed Playwright module if it is not on the project path. `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH`, `FABRIC_QA_URL` (default `http://localhost:5173`), and `FABRIC_QA_OUTPUT` are optional overrides. This is browser emulation; an actual mobile device remains a separate check.\n\nTypechecks and builds verify code and compilation. They do not prove live sign-in, provider registration, funded inference, checkout, wallet delivery or webhook reconciliation. Record those separately after exercising a registered account and configured deployment. A prompt dry run proves prompt drafting only.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"05f42444-7bf0-43d6-b81f-18d2c43372d6","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:14:18.174Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Local development\n\nUse Nix and Devenv from the repository root. Native tasks run npm scripts with Node and install frozen dependencies using the root and site `package-lock.json` files.\n\n```sh\ndevenv shell\ndevenv tasks run baste:install\ndevenv up\n```\n\n`devenv up` starts the Baste API on port 3456 and the Qwik site on port 5173. Open `http://localhost:5173/gui/` for the Studio or `http://localhost:5173/docs/` for documentation. The site proxies `/api` to the local API, keeping session cookies on one origin.\n\nThe bundled GUI served by `baste gui` is also available on the API port. It is a local legacy interface; the Qwik Studio owns the account, wallet and live hosted-model UI.\n\nIf the running site reports a missing import for a source file that now exists, restart just the site with `devenv processes restart site`. Vite can retain an SSR import failure when the importing file is updated before the new module is created. Check the rendered Studio and browser console after recovery: a development error page can return HTTP 200, so a successful health request alone does not verify the page.\n\n## Saved projects\n\nOpen **Projects** in the Studio to give an application a brief and choose an audience persona. Projects retain their own audience snapshot, so editing a source persona does not silently alter an existing project. Each saved change creates a revision; restoring an earlier revision creates a new history entry.\n\nLocal projects are stored in `.baste/projects`. Hosted projects use the signed-in Not Organic account's directory under `.baste/accounts`. These private runtime files are ignored by Git. Concurrent changes return a conflict so the Studio can retain the draft and offer the latest saved version. Repeated requests with the same command ID do not create duplicate changes.\n\nThis is the first milestone of the [design partner plan](plans/design-partner.md). Generated characters, conversational refinement, GPT-Live and stop-motion performance are subsequent milestones.\n\nAn interrupted writer can leave a project lock behind. If a saved project keeps reporting that it is busy after a server crash, stop every Baste process using that storage before repairing the specific lock. From the same working directory as the server, after building:\n\n```sh\ndevenv processes down\nnode dist/src/projects/repair-lock.js --project <project-id> --server-stopped\n# For a hosted project, also supply its owner's DID:\nnode dist/src/projects/repair-lock.js --project <project-id> --account <owner-did> --server-stopped\ndevenv up\n```\n\nThe repair preserves project history and command receipts. It refuses a live lock owner, a changed file or a symlink. The stopped-server precondition also covers other workers or replicas sharing this directory; run the appropriate local or hosted command once, then restart. This operation is deliberately unavailable to browser and agent callers.\n\n## Tasks\n\n| Task | Behavior |\n| --- | --- |\n| `baste:install` | Install root and site dependencies from their lockfiles |\n| `baste:api` | Start the Baste API |\n| `baste:site` | Start the Qwik site and Studio |\n| `baste:docs` | Start the site for its `/docs/` route |\n| `baste:storybook` | Start Storybook |\n| `baste:dev` | Start the configured development processes with `devenv up` |\n| `baste:build` | Build the CLI/package and site |\n| `baste:typecheck` | Check root and site TypeScript |\n| `baste:lint` | Check frontend lint rules |\n| `baste:test` | Run existing root tests |\n| `baste:check` | Run the configured validation tasks |\n| `baste:storybook:build` | Build the component explorer |\n\n```sh\ndevenv tasks list\ndevenv tasks run baste:typecheck\ndevenv tasks run baste:check\n```\n\nStorybook does not start by default. Enable its process when needed:\n\n```sh\nBASTE_WITH_STORYBOOK=1 devenv up\n```\n\n## Configuration\n\nCopy `.env.example` to `.env` and configure the providers you use. Do not commit `.env` or a config file containing private keys.\n\n- `BASTE_API_PORT`: API process port, default `3456`.\n- `BASTE_SITE_PORT`: Qwik development port, default `5173`.\n- `BASTE_STORYBOOK_PORT`: Storybook port, default `6006`.\n- `BASTE_WITH_STORYBOOK=1`: opt-in Storybook process.\n- `BASTE_PUBLIC_ORIGIN`: exact browser origin for account callbacks and CSRF checks. Devenv sets `http://localhost:5173`; the standalone API defaults to `http://localhost:3456`. Set it explicitly when running the Qwik Studio outside Devenv, changing its port or serving a deployed Studio.\n\nThe Studio uses `/api` by default. Its Settings connection field supports an explicit API URL for local development. Account mode requires the configured Studio origin and a same-origin proxy. A public static site needs its hosting layer to route `/api` to Baste; a static build alone does not provide the account API.\n\nFor local generation, configure `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `QUIVER_API_KEY`, `GOOGLE_API_KEY`, and any other selected provider's settings. Run `baste config --init` for a local `baste.config.json`. Preview prompts with `baste generate cyberbotanist --dry-run` before spending provider credit.\n\nThe public persona conversation at `/#meet` uses authored replies when no conversation model is available. In local mode, `OPENAI_API_KEY` enables open-ended replies through `POST /api/converse/:id`; `BASTE_CONVERSATION_MODEL` selects the model (default `gpt-4o`). Restart the API after changing these values. `/api/health` reports `conversation.mode` as `ai` or `demo`. Account mode always disables this local-key path. Hosted AI conversation still needs a metered account transport; the public page labels its authored demo explicitly. Failed AI replies remain visible with a retry action, and never silently become demo replies.\n\nTechnical explanations, scoring, exports and local setup are at `/method/`. The public landing page introduces the personas. Lenis and Tempus run only on the landing and Method pages; inner chat and Studio scrollers remain native. The Method page's decorative Strands composition from shaders.com loads on visibility, with a static fallback for unavailable WebGPU and reduced motion. The heading reveal adapts React Bits' BlurText treatment to Qwik without adding a React runtime.\n\nThe public conversation reuses the Moss, Ren and Ada portraits from the October 8 companion workroom studies, recovered from worktree `73bc` through the local Entire session history. Their source prompts and asset provenance are in [companion-portraits.json](companion-portraits.json). They are illustrated example characters; the page does not claim that runtime portrait generation or the full Studio partner workflow is implemented. The conversation keeps the atelier typography and writing surface stable, while palette and type samples show each persona's design choices inline.\n\nFor the hosted account path, see [Not Organic integration](notorganic.md). Local CLI calls do not receive a browser's hosted account session.\n\n## Verification boundaries\n\nThe fabric regression check exercises window resizing, a lost WebGL context, and touch viewport changes while scrolling. It checks that no resized canvas reaches paint before being redrawn, inspects the rendered background, and saves screenshots plus a report under `/tmp/baste-fabric-qa`:\n\n```sh\nrtk proxy node site/scripts/verify-fabric.mjs\n```\n\nSet `PLAYWRIGHT_MODULE` to an installed Playwright module if it is not on the project path. `PLAYWRIGHT_CHROMIUM_EXECUTABLE_PATH`, `FABRIC_QA_URL` (default `http://localhost:5173`), and `FABRIC_QA_OUTPUT` are optional overrides. This is browser emulation; an actual mobile device remains a separate check.\n\nTypechecks and builds verify code and compilation. They do not prove live sign-in, provider registration, funded inference, checkout, wallet delivery or webhook reconciliation. Record those separately after exercising a registered account and configured deployment. A prompt dry run proves prompt drafting only.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"baa3ca72-a108-4c49-a264-cd75255633d0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
