{"parentUuid":"89cf21da-80bc-4b58-93fa-0d671f9be140","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4f5ed931-9f1d-475a-be32-8d6a81df3ec7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013r35RHeXArb1NcyHTsohmU","type":"tool_result","content":"@layer base {\n  :root {\n    --paper: #F1ECE2;\n    --ink: #1C1B19;\n    --thread: #D2402A;\n    --chalk: #2F55A4;\n    --rule: #CFC7B8;\n    --grid: rgba(28, 27, 25, 0.045);\n    --ease-thread: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);\n    color-scheme: light;\n  }\n  /* Paper remains without WebGL; the SVG drafting grid in FabricBackdrop\n     renders independently of the live linen. */\n  html {\n    scroll-behavior: smooth;\n    color: var(--ink);\n    -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;\n    background-color: var(--paper);\n  }\n  body {\n    font-family: 'Instrument Sans', 'Helvetica Neue', system-ui, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 16px;\n    line-height: 1.55;\n    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;\n    -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;\n    min-height: 100vh;\n    background: transparent;\n  }\n  ::selection {\n    background: #F0C534;\n    color: var(--ink);\n  }\n  :focus-visible {\n    outline: 2px solid var(--chalk);\n    outline-offset: 2px;\n    border-radius: 2px;\n  }\n  a { color: inherit; }\n  /* Didone display face: tighten at size, let the optical axis do its work */\n  .display {\n    font-family: 'Bodoni Moda', 'Bodoni Moda Fallback', 'Didot', Georgia, serif;\n    font-optical-sizing: auto;\n    font-weight: 500;\n    letter-spacing: -0.02em;\n    line-height: 0.98;\n  }\n  .label {\n    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;\n    font-size: 11px;\n    font-weight: 500;\n    letter-spacing: 0.12em;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n  }\n  .skip-link {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 12px;\n    top: -60px;\n    z-index: 100;\n    padding: 8px 14px;\n    background: var(--ink);\n    color: var(--paper);\n    border-radius: 4px;\n    text-decoration: none;\n  }\n  .skip-link:focus { top: 12px; }","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1b61d3e3-2070-4867-9940-d91b95e73c7e","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:14:27.819Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"@layer base {\n  :root {\n    --paper: #F1ECE2;\n    --ink: #1C1B19;\n    --thread: #D2402A;\n    --chalk: #2F55A4;\n    --rule: #CFC7B8;\n    --grid: rgba(28, 27, 25, 0.045);\n    --ease-thread: cubic-bezier(0.22, 1, 0.36, 1);\n    color-scheme: light;\n  }\n  /* Paper remains without WebGL; the SVG drafting grid in FabricBackdrop\n     renders independently of the live linen. */\n  html {\n    scroll-behavior: smooth;\n    color: var(--ink);\n    -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;\n    background-color: var(--paper);\n  }\n  body {\n    font-family: 'Instrument Sans', 'Helvetica Neue', system-ui, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 16px;\n    line-height: 1.55;\n    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;\n    -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;\n    min-height: 100vh;\n    background: transparent;\n  }\n  ::selection {\n    background: #F0C534;\n    color: var(--ink);\n  }\n  :focus-visible {\n    outline: 2px solid var(--chalk);\n    outline-offset: 2px;\n    border-radius: 2px;\n  }\n  a { color: inherit; }\n  /* Didone display face: tighten at size, let the optical axis do its work */\n  .display {\n    font-family: 'Bodoni Moda', 'Bodoni Moda Fallback', 'Didot', Georgia, serif;\n    font-optical-sizing: auto;\n    font-weight: 500;\n    letter-spacing: -0.02em;\n    line-height: 0.98;\n  }\n  .label {\n    font-family: 'IBM Plex Mono', ui-monospace, monospace;\n    font-size: 11px;\n    font-weight: 500;\n    letter-spacing: 0.12em;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n  }\n  .skip-link {\n    position: absolute;\n    left: 12px;\n    top: -60px;\n    z-index: 100;\n    padding: 8px 14px;\n    background: var(--ink);\n    color: var(--paper);\n    border-radius: 4px;\n    text-decoration: none;\n  }\n  .skip-link:focus { top: 12px; }","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"89cf21da-80bc-4b58-93fa-0d671f9be140","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/site","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"1b61d3e3-2070-4867-9940-d91b95e73c7e","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"environment","snapshot":{"workingDirectory":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/site","isWorktree":false,"isGitRepo":true,"additionalWorkingDirectories":["/home/diogenes/.t3/userdata/attachments"],"platform":"linux","shell":"bash","osVersion":"Linux 6.19.14-108.fc42.x86_64"},"changes":[{"field":"workingDirectory","from":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"e6d84d25-3151-474e-a8fc-5b65e17b7b99","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:14:27.844Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n# Environment update\n - Primary working directory: /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/site (was /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste)\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/site","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"e6d84d25-3151-474e-a8fc-5b65e17b7b99","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfzvn3Dibi7HF5bSxaQGz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm noticing a specificity conflict: guide.css sets a pointer cursor on buttons directly, which breaks the rule that components shouldn't set cursor themselves, since both the global cursor vocabulary and guide.css are unlayered, so this override would win and clobber the pin cursor.\n\nSince the global rules already assign the pin cursor to buttons and summary elements, removing that guide.css line restores consistency without affecting functionality—my new clip button isn't inside .guide-watch anyway, so I'll remove it and note the fix.\n\nNow I'm moving on to writing the TourSection component...\n\nWriting section markup...\n\nI'm also adding a thin progress rail above the chapter strip that fills based on playback position, and weighing accessibility details like whether `aria-current` should be \"true\" or \"step\" for the active chapter button, plus crafting a clearer accessible label like \"Measure, at 0:09\" instead of just concatenating the time and title.\n\nNow I'm writing the play handler, which sets the video's current time if a target timestamp was given, marks playback as started, and calls play while catching any rejected promise so the controls remain usable. I'm also considering how `preload=\"none\"` interacts with setting `currentTime` before the video has loaded, since readyState 0 in Chrome triggers implicit loading behavior.\n\nI'm wiring up `controls={started.value}` to show native controls once playback begins, and an `onPlay$` handler to cover starting via keyboard or native controls too, plus an `onTimeUpdate$` that syncs the time signal using Qwik's `(event, element)` handler signature. For passing the play function down to a `TourChapters` child, I'm treating it as a QRL prop like `onSeek$={play}` so the child can trigger seeking in the parent.\n\nActually, I'm reconsidering splitting into a child component at all — re-rendering a small video page 4 times a second is trivial for Qwik's vdom diffing, so I'll just keep everything in one component for simplicity. Now I'm writing the logic to compute which chapter is currently active based on the current playback time.\n\nI also need to figure out how the progress rail should show nothing before the tour starts, and I'm checking that Qwik supports CSS custom properties like `--p` directly in style objects for the progress indicator.\n\nWriting tour layout CSS...\n\nStill writing video player styles...\n\nStill writing styles...\n\nI'm envisioning the chapter strip as a ruler with a stitched-thread top line, tick marks at each chapter start, and mono-font timestamps with active chapters in bold ink and inactive ones muted. For mobile, I'm switching the chapters to a two-column grid, accepting that the top progress line won't perfectly align with chapter positions anymore.\n\nFor scrollable mobile layouts, I realize computing per-chapter progress fills individually solves the alignment problem better than a single absolute progress bar spanning the scroll container.\n\nI'm also considering background treatment for the tour section — whether to keep the linen backdrop visible through transparency or introduce a deeper paper tone to separate it from the hero.\n\nActually, a darker \"screening room\" band with ink background feels like the stronger choice — it gives the video a cinema-like pop and a sense of \"lights down\" drama, with tape-yellow labels, paper headline text, and thread-red emphasis checked for contrast against the dark background.\n\nI'm also confirming the earlier flicker/resize bug on the fabric backdrop is already resolved and won't conflict with a dark band, and weighing how this fits the site's existing use of ink as a brand color for dark elements like buttons.\n\nChecking contrast ratios: paper text on ink is very high contrast, muted text is solid, but the red thread color is borderline for small text so I should reserve it for large headings or non-text elements, using the tape yellow instead for small details like chapter timestamps and for focus rings on dark backgrounds.\n\nNative video controls look fine on the dark band, but I'm now worried about the custom needle cursor SVG — if it's dark ink without a light outline, it would vanish against the dark section, so I need to check the actual SVG file and see whether a light variant exists for dark surfaces.\n\nThe thread-cursor trailing effect follows the needle in red, which should still read fine on dark — but I should verify needle.svg and pin.svg directly to confirm their contrast.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1053,"cache_read_input_tokens":259935,"output_tokens":5992,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":5716},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1053,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5992,"cache_read_input_tokens":259935,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1053,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1053},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":57629,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5a40cb0b-a687-4bd1-9973-db76bcb57295","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:15:27.906Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/site","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
