ach. The vision judge defaults to <code>google/gemini-2.5-flash</code>; SVG markup and video prompts go to the text endpoint because the vision endpoint needs an image. In the Studio, choose <strong>fal (images, icons and judge)</strong> as the image provider. A run fails at the start when <code>FAL_KEY</code> is missing, before anything is spent.</p>\n            <p class={prose}>Draft with <code>--dry-run</code> first. Each stage bills your fal account, and judging adds a request for every candidate, so iterations and batch size multiply the cost.</p>\n          </section>\n\n          <section id=\"voice\" class={section}>\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"            <p class={prose}>The quality-diversity archive explores color temperature, visual density and abstractness. Judging weights persona alignment at 30%, visual quality and uniqueness at 20% each, coherence and usability at 15% each. These scores guide selection; review assets in the interface they will serve.</p>\n          </section>\"\"\",\n\"\"\"            <p class={prose}>The quality-diversity archive explores color temperature, visual density and abstractness. Judging weights persona alignment at 30%, visual quality and uniqueness at 20% each, coherence and usability at 15% each. These scores guide selection; review assets in the interface they will serve.</p>\n          </section>\n\n          <section id=\"tour\" class={section}>\n            <h2 class={title}>Rebuild the tour video</h2>\n            <p class={prose}>The 74-second tour on the home page and in the Studio guide is a <a href=\"https://hyperframes.heygen.com/\">HyperFrames</a> composition in <code>videos/baste-tour/</code>. Every screen in it is recorded from this site, and the archive replays a real fal run. Each stage writes files the next one reads, so you can redo one step without the others.</p>\n            <CodeView label=\"Tour pipeline\" code={'# 1 · Record the screens (site on :5173, system Chrome on the GPU)\\nnode scripts/record-tour.mjs\\n\\n# 2 · Narration and music on fal (ElevenLabs voice, Whisper timings, Stable Audio bed)\\nnode scripts/narrate-tour.mjs --skate\\nnode scripts/score-tour.mjs --skate\\n\\n# 3 · Compose, check, render, publish\\ncd videos/baste-tour\\nnode build.mjs\\nnpx hyperframes@0.8.145 check\\nnpx hyperframes@0.8.145 render --quality high --fps 30 --output renders/baste-tour.mp4\\nnode publish.mjs'} />\n            <p class={prose}><code>build.mjs</code> holds the edit: which seconds of each recording play, at what speed, and where the camera moves. It writes the composition, levels the voice lines, and makes English and French captions; the French lines are in <code>narration/captions.fr.json</code>. <code>publish.mjs</code> encodes the web video, poster and the Studio guide’s chapter clips into <code>site/public/media/tour/</code>, and writes <code>site/src/lib/tour.json</code> for the chapter list and transcript.</p>\n            <p class={prose}>The narration and music scripts read <code>FAL_KEY</code>, or take it from Skate with <code>--skate</code>; the key is never written to a file. On a Nix or Guix host, run the recorder and the HyperFrames commands with <code>env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH</code> so Chrome loads the system libraries, and put the system <code>ldd</code> first on <code>PATH</code> for the render preflight. A render is cancelled when its launching shell exits; set <code>HYPERFRAMES_RENDER_DETACHED=1</code> to run it detached.</p>\n          </section>\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"id=\\\"fal\\\"\\|id=\\\"tour\\\"\" src/routes/docs/developers/index.tsx","description":"Document the fal provider and tour pipeline for developers"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8e40f1c1-0c63-4188-82c5-b1af4dc9726a","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:20:30.608Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-