    <p class={prose}>With <code>FAL_KEY</code> set, one fal account can cover a whole run: Seedream v4 images, Recraft v3 vector icons, Seedance 1 Pro ambient loops, and a judge that looks at the rendered images through fal’s vision model. The archive in the <a href=\"/#tour\">tour</a> came from a run like this.</p>","+            <CodeView label=\"Generate on fal\" code={'FAL_KEY=… baste generate cyberbotanist --provider fal","+","+# Mix providers: fal images, your QuiverAI SVGs, OpenAI judging","+baste generate cyberbotanist --image-provider fal --svg-provider quiver --judge openai'} />","+            <p class={prose}><code>--provider fal</code> routes every stage through fal; <code>--image-provider</code>, <code>--svg-provider</code>, <code>--video-provider</code> and <code>--judge</code> override one stage each. The vision judge defaults to <code>google/gemini-2.5-flash</code>; SVG markup and video prompts go to the text endpoint because the vision endpoint needs an image. In the Studio, choose <strong>fal (images, icons and judge)</strong> as the image provider. A run fails at the start when <code>FAL_KEY</code> is missing, before anything is spent.</p>","+            <p class={prose}>Draft with <code>--dry-run</code> first. Each stage bills your fal account, and judging adds a request for every candidate, so iterations and batch size multiply the cost.</p>","+          </section>","+","           <section id=\"voice\" class={section}>","             <h2 class={title}>Companion voice</h2>","             <p class={prose}>Set <code>FAL_KEY</code> on the Baste API server for ElevenLabs Turbo v2.5 speech and Wizper transcription. The browser sends recorded audio to Baste and receives audio bytes or editable text; it never receives the provider key. Recording starts only after a user gesture and stops after 45 seconds.</p>"]},{"oldStart":90,"oldLines":6,"newStart":102,"newLines":26,"lines":["             <CodeView label=\"Local asset output structure\" code={'assets/output/\\n  svg/\\n  images/\\n  videos/\\n  {persona}-suite.json'} />","             <p class={prose}>The quality-diversity archive explores color temperature, visual density and abstractness. Judging weights persona alignment at 30%, visual quality and uniqueness at 20% each, coherence and usability at 15% each. These scores guide selection; review assets in the interface they will serve.</p>","           </section>","+","+          <section id=\"tour\" class={section}>","+            <h2 class={title}>Rebuild the tour video</h2>","+            <p class={prose}>The 74-second tour on the home page and in the Studio guide is a <a href=\"https://hyperframes.heygen.com/\">HyperFrames</a> composition in <code>videos/baste-tour/</code>. Every screen in it is recorded from this site, and the archive replays a real fal run. Each stage writes files the next one reads, so you can redo one step without the others.</p>","+            <CodeView label=\"Tour pipeline\" code={'# 1 · Record the screens (site on :5173, system Chrome on the GPU)","+node scripts/record-tour.mjs","+","+# 2 · Narration and music on fal (ElevenLabs voice, Whisper timings, Stable Audio bed)","+node scripts/narrate-tour.mjs --skate","+node scripts/score-tour.mjs --skate","+","+# 3 · Compose, check, render, publish","+cd videos/baste-tour","+node build.mjs","+npx hyperframes@0.8.145 check","+npx hyperframes@0.8.145 render --quality high --fps 30 --output renders/baste-tour.mp4","+node publish.mjs'} />","+            <p class={prose}><code>build.mjs</code> holds the edit: which seconds of each recording play, at what speed, and where the camera moves. It writes the composition, levels the voice lines, and makes English and French captions; the French lines are in <code>narration/captions.fr.json</code>. <code>publish.mjs</code> encodes the web video, poster and the Studio guide’s chapter clips into <code>site/public/media/tour/</code>, and writes <code>site/src/lib/tour.json</code> for the chapter list and transcript.</p>","+            <p class={prose}>The narration and music scripts read <code>FAL_KEY</code>, or take it from Skate with <code>--skate</code>; the key is never written to a file. On a Nix or Guix host, run the recorder and the HyperFrames commands with <code>env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH</code> so Chrome loads the system libraries, and put the system <code>ldd</code> first on <code>PATH</code> for the render preflight. A render is cancelled when its launching shell exits; set <code>HYPERFRAMES_RENDER_DETACHED=1</code> to run it detached.</p>","+          </section>","         </div>","       </div>","     </main>"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/site/src/routes/docs/developers/index.tsx"]}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8e40f1c1-0c63-4188-82c5-b1af4dc9726a","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/site","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
