{"parentUuid":"31c506b9-ebbc-4855-8f34-67ae21ef340b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzwFLmAUhwNZaxrPj28w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The model names in the docs match the scripts. Now updating `README.md` and `docs/development.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":651,"cache_read_input_tokens":278711,"output_tokens":1809,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":651,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1809,"cache_read_input_tokens":278711,"cache_creation_input_tokens":651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":651},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c11a66b3-e519-4e26-93ec-c6b7bf5e0689","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:20:41.078Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"c11a66b3-e519-4e26-93ec-c6b7bf5e0689","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzwFLmAUhwNZaxrPj28w","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RT3xPsruvZmHbHubgK787q","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep(\"\"\"![One interface, fitted to three personas](docs/fitting-loop.gif)\n\"\"\",\"\"\"![One interface, fitted to three personas](docs/fitting-loop.gif)\n\n**[Watch the 74-second tour](site/public/media/tour/baste-tour.mp4)**: measure a person, re-cut one screen for\nthree people, judge two dozen drafts, keep the files. It plays on the site's home page and in the Studio guide\n(`/docs/`), with English and French captions.\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"# Dry run (see prompts without calling APIs)\nbaste generate cyberbotanist --dry-run\n\"\"\",\"\"\"# Dry run (see prompts without calling APIs)\nbaste generate cyberbotanist --dry-run\n\n# One fal key for everything: Seedream images, Recraft SVG, Seedance video, a vision judge\nbaste generate cyberbotanist --provider fal\n\n# Or choose per stage\nbaste generate cyberbotanist --image-provider fal --svg-provider quiver --judge openai\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIza...     # Gemini images / Veo video (optional)\n```\n\"\"\",\"\"\"GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIza...     # Gemini images / Veo video (optional)\nFAL_KEY=...                # fal: --provider fal for every stage, and companion voice\n```\n\n## The tour video\n\nThe tour is a [HyperFrames](https://hyperframes.heygen.com/) composition in `videos/baste-tour/`, cut from\nscreens recorded on this site. `scripts/record-tour.mjs` records them, `scripts/narrate-tour.mjs` and\n`scripts/score-tour.mjs` make the narration and music on fal, `build.mjs` composes it, and `publish.mjs` puts the\nvideo, captions and the Studio guide's chapter clips into `site/public/media/tour/`. See\n[local development](docs/development.md#tour-video) for the commands.\n\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='docs/development.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"## Verification boundaries\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"## Tour video\n\nThe 74-second tour on the home page and in the Studio guide is a HyperFrames composition in `videos/baste-tour/`. Each step writes files the next one reads, so any step can be redone alone:\n\n```sh\n# Screens, recorded from the running site with the system Chrome on the GPU\nenv -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH node scripts/record-tour.mjs        # footage/*.webm, clips.json, cfr/*.mp4\n# Narration (ElevenLabs Aria, fal Whisper word timings) and the music bed (Stable Audio 2.5), all on fal\nnode scripts/narrate-tour.mjs --skate                       # narration/\nnode scripts/score-tour.mjs --skate                         # music/bed.mp3\ncd videos/baste-tour\nnode build.mjs                                              # index.html, captions.vtt, captions.fr.vtt, assets/voice/\nenv -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH npx --yes hyperframes@0.8.145 check\nenv -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH npx --yes hyperframes@0.8.145 snapshot --at 20,43,60\nenv -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH npx --yes hyperframes@0.8.145 render --quality high --fps 30 --output renders/baste-tour.mp4\nnode publish.mjs                                            # site/public/media/tour/, site/src/lib/tour.json\n```\n\n`build.mjs` holds the edit: the seconds of each recording that play, their speed, the wipes and the camera moves. It refuses a cut that starts before 3.6 s, while the development overlay is still on screen, or that runs past the end of a take. French subtitles live in `narration/captions.fr.json`, one line per English cue; the build stops if the counts differ. `--skate` reads `fal_api_key@secrets`; otherwise set `FAL_KEY`. The key is only held in the process.\n\nThe render's preflight runs `ldd` on its Chrome. On a Nix or Guix host, unset `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` and put the system `ldd` first on `PATH` (for example a directory holding a link to `/usr/bin/ldd`). A render is cancelled when the shell that launched it exits; set `HYPERFRAMES_RENDER_DETACHED=1` to run one in the background. Footage, renders, snapshots and `.work/` are build products and stay out of Git; the published files under `site/public/media/tour/` are what the site serves.\n\n## Verification boundaries\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new); open(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"## Tour video\\|## The tour video\" README.md docs/development.md","description":"Add the tour and fal provider to the README and dev guide"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":651,"cache_read_input_tokens":278711,"output_tokens":1809,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":651,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1809,"cache_read_input_tokens":278711,"cache_creation_input_tokens":651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":651},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RT3xPsruvZmHbHubgK787q":{"command":"cd /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste && python3 - <<'EOF'\np='README.md'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep(\"\"\"![One interface, fitted to three personas](docs/fitting-loop.gif)\n\"\"\",\"\"\"![One interface, fitted to three personas](docs/fitting-loop.gif)\n\n**[Watch the 74-second tour](site/public/media/tour/baste-tour.mp4)**: measure a person, re-cut one screen for\nthree people, judge two dozen drafts, keep the files. It plays on the site's home page and in the Studio guide\n(`/docs/`), with English and French captions.\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"# Dry run (see prompts without calling APIs)\nbaste generate cyberbotanist --dry-run\n\"\"\",\"\"\"# Dry run (see prompts without calling APIs)\nbaste generate cyberbotanist --dry-run\n\n# One fal key for everything: Seedream images, Recraft SVG, Seedance video, a vision judge\nbaste generate cyberbotanist --provider fal\n\n# Or choose per stage\nbaste generate cyberbotanist --image-provider fal --svg-provider quiver --judge openai\n\"\"\")\nrep(\"\"\"GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIza...     # Gemini images / Veo video (optional)\n```\n\"\"\",\"\"\"GOOGLE_API_KEY=AIza...     # Gemini images / Veo video (optional)\nFAL_KEY=...                # fal: --provider fal for every stage, and companion voice\n```\n\n## The tour video\n\nThe tour is a [HyperFrames](https://hyperframes.heygen.com/) composition in `videos/baste-tour/`, cut from\nscreens recorded on this site. `scripts/record-tour.mjs` records them, `scripts/narrate-tour.mjs` and\n`scripts/score-tour.mjs` make the narration and music on fal, `build.mjs` composes it, and `publish.mjs` puts the\nvideo, captions and the Studio guide's chapter clips into `site/public/media/tour/`. See\n[local development](docs/development.md#tour-video) for the commands.\n\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='docs/development.md'; s=open(p).read()\nold=\"\"\"## Verification boundaries\"\"\"\nnew=\"\"\"## Tour video\n\nThe 74-second tour on the home page and in the Studio guide is a HyperFrames composition in `videos/baste-tour/`. Each step writes files the next one reads, so any step can be redone alone:\n\n```sh\n# Screens, recorded from the running site with the system Chrome on the GPU\nenv -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH node scripts/record-tour.mjs        # footage/*.webm, clips.json, cfr/*.mp4\n# Narration (ElevenLabs Aria, fal Whisper word timings) and the music bed (Stable Audio 2.5), all on fal\nnode scripts/narrate-tour.mjs --skate                       # narration/\nnode scripts/score-tour.mjs --skate                         # music/bed.mp3\ncd videos/baste-tour\nnode build.mjs                                              # index.html, captions.vtt, captions.fr.vtt, assets/voice/\nenv -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH npx --yes hyperframes@0.8.145 check\nenv -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH npx --yes hyperframes@0.8.145 snapshot --at 20,43,60\nenv -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH npx --yes hyperframes@0.8.145 render --quality high --fps 30 --output renders/baste-tour.mp4\nnode publish.mjs                                            # site/public/media/tour/, site/src/lib/tour.json\n```\n\n`build.mjs` holds the edit: the seconds of each recording that play, their speed, the wipes and the camera moves. It refuses a cut that starts before 3.6 s, while the development overlay is still on screen, or that runs past the end of a take. French subtitles live in `narration/captions.fr.json`, one line per English cue; the build stops if the counts differ. `--skate` reads `fal_api_key@secrets`; otherwise set `FAL_KEY`. The key is only held in the process.\n\nThe render's preflight runs `ldd` on its Chrome. On a Nix or Guix host, unset `LD_LIBRARY_PATH` and put the system `ldd` first on `PATH` (for example a directory holding a link to `/usr/bin/ldd`). A render is cancelled when the shell that launched it exits; set `HYPERFRAMES_RENDER_DETACHED=1` to run one in the background. Footage, renders, snapshots and `.work/` are build products and stay out of Git; the published files under `site/public/media/tour/` are what the site serves.\n\n## Verification boundaries\"\"\"\nassert s.count(old)==1; s=s.replace(old,new); open(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -n \"## Tour video\\|## The tour video\" README.md docs/development.md","description":"Add the tour and fal provider to the README and dev guide"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01RT3xPsruvZmHbHubgK787q":{"cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3d948bfd-0ef0-49bf-849f-cf10aa9