{"parentUuid":"6f0a8568-9d13-41d9-a994-18629e35dc54","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzwHo9TrcxqRUXLAX3ML","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"footage-v1 is a 157 MB gitignored leftover from an earlier recording take, and bed-source.wav is a 13 MB audio file mentioned in the cleanup summary. Since deleting is irreversible, I should be cautious even though footage-v1 looks like a safe build artifact from my own prior session.\n\nSince the folder is already ignored by git, there's no real downside to keeping it besides disk space, so I'll leave it in place and just note in the final report that it's safe to delete. Now I'll move on to re-running checks: QA screenshots of the tour section after the figcaption fix, the developer docs page, type checking, lint, root tests, and the site build, plus verifying the tour hover link color and play button styling.\n\nChecking the cursor system for buttons, I confirm the needle SVG's paper outline stroke stays visible against the dark band. I also notice the tour section uses `data-scroll` to set `--scene`, but since my CSS doesn't reference that variable, I'll strip it out to avoid unnecessary per-frame work, while leaving `data-words` on the h2 since it's needed for the sew-in reveal animation. The button and controls logic look correct — no native controls before start since the big play button covers it, and both play and chapter buttons are real buttons for keyboard accessibility.\n\nOn mobile at 390px width, chapter names like \"Fitting room\" truncate because the flex-basis of 11px per second isn't wide enough; recalculating durations against font width, I bump the multiplier to 13px per second and add a minimum width of 116px to keep every label readable. I also want to verify the chapter progress rule at 1440px correctly fills only up through the current chapter's position rather than overshooting.\n\nChecking the transcript formatting and the French translation for the tour button label, both look correct, aside from a pre-existing untranslated \"Narrated tour · English\" string. The 500 errors from QA trace back to the health-check proxy failing because no API server is running locally, which is unrelated to my changes. I'll apply the CSS tweaks now and rerun QA for the tour section at 390px and the developer docs page.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1445,"cache_read_input_tokens":281618,"output_tokens":2523,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1568},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1445,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2523,"cache_read_input_tokens":281618,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1445,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1445},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":19158,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5548ecfe-80af-4c80-85e8-f2b0b19168fa","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:21:33.180Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
