{"parentUuid":"106e5e89-f51f-4a7c-bf56-70baaa2b3dbf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzwXmvBsGx22EJrMtbF1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This failing test traces back to recorded-runs.ts using a Vite-only glob feature, which seems to be from earlier work rather than my current changes — likely created in an earlier session as part of the recorded fal run replay feature.\n\nI'm trying to figure out how to make this glob call resilient outside Vite's build context, but since `import.meta.glob` is a compile-time transform that Vite statically rewrites, wrapping it in conditional checks like `typeof` guards won't work reliably — Vite's static analysis only recognizes the direct call pattern, so any indirection risks breaking the actual browser build while trying to fix the test runner.\n\nA cleaner path is to make the import of recorded-runs.ts lazy — dynamically importing it only when replay actually happens, so the test suite never evaluates that module unless it's needed. I want to check whether demo-client.ts only needs recorded-runs synchronously or could tolerate an async import, and I should check git status to see if I introduced this breakage myself when adding recorded-runs.ts earlier in this session.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1269,"cache_read_input_tokens":284188,"output_tokens":1328,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1132},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1269,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1328,"cache_read_input_tokens":284188,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1269,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1269},"type":"messag