{"parentUuid":"a3fb69b9-ba73-4fb6-b66a-1ef1a0896916","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"4f5ed931-9f1d-475a-be32-8d6a81df3ec7","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MPsvoqaHFYmFufCoWA8btn"}]},"uuid":"93f38b12-4497-496f-882c-cc8f988642d1","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:26:30.889Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 1","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a3fb69b9-ba73-4fb6-b66a-1ef1a0896916","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/videos/baste-tour","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"93f38b12-4497-496f-882c-cc8f988642d1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfzwhWJ85iyBXrcbxJGAg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AskHAjaRkFVJSzwcmxMpQH","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/home/diogenes/.claude/projects/-home-diogenes-Projects-apps-baste/memory/hyperframes-render-env.md","content":"---\nname: hyperframes-render-env\ndescription: How to run HyperFrames check/snapshot/render on this nix/guix Fedora host without Chrome or watchdog failures\nmetadata:\n  type: reference\n---\n\nHyperFrames (pinned `hyperframes@0.8.145`, project `videos/baste-tour/`) needs three workarounds here:\n\n- Prefix every command with `env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH`. The shell's LD_LIBRARY_PATH holds nix alsa-lib plus a T3 AppImage mount, which breaks Chrome.\n- The render preflight runs `ldd`, and guix's `ldd` reports missing libs. Keep a shim at `~/.cache/hf-shim/ldd -> /usr/bin/ldd` (not /tmp, which T3 restarts wipe) and put it first on PATH.\n- A render is cancelled (\"render_cancelled_parent_exited\") when its launching shell exits, and T3 restarts kill background shells. Launch detached:\n  `HYPERFRAMES_RENDER_DETACHED=1 setsid nohup bash -c 'env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH PATH=$HOME/.cache/hf-shim:$PATH npx --yes hyperframes@0.8.145 render ... > renders/render.log 2>&1; echo \"exit $?\" >> renders/render.log' &`\n  then wait with an until-loop on `^exit ` in the log.\n\nWith `--workers 8` the 74 s tour renders in about 90 s once Chrome starts.\n\nRelated: [[baste-dev-servers]]\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":296,"cache_read_input_tokens":284529,"output_tokens":2021,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":296,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2021,"cache_read_input_tokens":284529,"cache_creation_input_tokens":296,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":296},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01AskHAjaRkFVJSzwcmxMpQH":{"file_path":"/home/diogenes/.claude/projects/-home-diogenes-Projects-apps-baste/memory/hyperframes-render-env.md","content":"---\nname: hyperframes-render-env\ndescription: How to run HyperFrames check/snapshot/render on this nix/guix Fedora host without Chrome or watchdog failures\nmetadata:\n  type: reference\n---\n\nHyperFrames (pinned `hyperframes@0.8.145`, project `videos/baste-tour/`) needs three workarounds here:\n\n- Prefix every command with `env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH`. The shell's LD_LIBRARY_PATH holds nix alsa-lib plus a T3 AppImage mount, which breaks Chrome.\n- The render preflight runs `ldd`, and guix's `ldd` reports missing libs. Keep a shim at `~/.cache/hf-shim/ldd -> /usr/bin/ldd` (not /tmp, which T3 restarts wipe) and put it first on PATH.\n- A render is cancelled (\"render_cancelled_parent_exited\") when its launching shell exits, and T3 restarts kill background shells. Launch detached:\n  `HYPERFRAMES_RENDER_DETACHED=1 setsid nohup bash -c 'env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH PATH=$HOME/.cache/hf-shim:$PATH npx --yes hyperframes@0.8.145 render ... > renders/render.log 2>&1; echo \"exit $?\" >> renders/render.log' &`\n  then wait with an until-loop on `^exit ` in the log.\n\nWith `--workers 8` the 74 s tour renders in about 90 s once Chrome starts.\n\nRelated: [[baste-dev-servers]]\n"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"5b145642-5120-479b-9c48-11e6e4fbf74e","timestamp":"2026-10-13T21:26:41.461Z","effort":"max","perTurnEffort":"max","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps