{"parentUuid":"6d03686a-dbf8-4bf0-9507-cbf2a5cc0481","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1MyXTJksr6jXkx39xVu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HYg8zxj62FUtPQHRoZDdAX","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://docs.cartesia.ai/api-reference/tts/bytes","prompt":"Give the exact endpoint, required headers (including Cartesia-Version current value), request body fields (model_id options, voice, output_format, language, generation_config/speed/emotion), and any example."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":293063,"output_tokens":357,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":201},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":632,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":357,"cache_read_input_tokens":293063,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":632},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HYg8zxj62FUtPQHRoZDdAX":{"url":"https://docs.cartesia.ai/api-reference/tts/bytes","prompt":"Give the exact endpoint, required headers (including Cartesia-Version current value), request body fields (model_id options, voice, output_format, language, generation_config/speed/emotion), and any example."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"bbb72041-49f1-412a-9782-50bce1ae36d0","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:45:01.516Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"bbb72041-49f1-412a-9782-50bce1ae36d0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1165d7a1-30cf-4c4e-a93c-fed0ec3c3592","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HYg8zxj62FUtPQHRoZDdAX","type":"tool_result","content":"# Cartesia TTS (Bytes)\n\n**Endpoint:** `POST https://api.cartesia.ai/tts/bytes`. It returns streamed audio bytes (`audio/*`, binary).\n\n## Required headers\n- **`Cartesia-Version`**: The only allowed value, and the default, is `2026-08-14`.\n- **`Authorization: Bearer <token>`**: Use either an API key (`sk_car_...`, from play.cartesia.ai/keys) or a short-lived JWT access token for client-side use.\n- **`Content-Type: application/json`**\n\n## Request body\n\n**Required fields:** `model_id`, `transcript`, `voice`, `output_format`\n\n- **`model_id`**: One of `sonic-3.6` (default), `sonic-3.5`, `sonic-3` or `sonic-latest`.\n- **`transcript`**: A string. The default is \"Hi there, it's awesome to meet you.\"\n- **`voice`**: Either a voice ID string or an object with a required `id`. The docs note that \"Embeddings are not accepted in this API version.\"\n- **`output_format`**: Choose one of these containers:\n  - **`wav`**: `encoding` (default `pcm_s16le`) and `sample_rate` (default 44100).\n  - **`mp3`**: `sample_rate` and `bit_rate` are both required. `bit_rate` is 32000, 64000, 96000, 128000 or 192000, with 128000 as the default.\n  - **`raw`**: `encoding` and `sample_rate` are both required.\n  - **Encodings:** `pcm_f32le`, `pcm_s16le`, `pcm_mulaw`, `pcm_alaw`.\n  - **Sample rates:** 8000, 16000, 22050, 24000, 44100, 48000.\n- **`language` / `locale`** (optional): Accepts codes like `en` or `en-GB`. Use only one of the two: \"setting both returns a 400 error.\"\n- **`accent`** (optional): Normally not needed. Use it only to give a multilingual voice an accent. The value must be one of the voice's listed `accents`.\n- **`normalization`** (optional): `auto` (default), `off`, or a language/locale code.\n- **`pronunciation_dict_id`** (optional): Works with `sonic-3` and newer models.\n- **`generation_config`** (optional, `sonic-3` and newer):\n  - **`volume`**: 0.5 to 2.0, default 1.\n  - **`speed`**: 0.6 to 1.5, default 1.\n  - **`emotion`**: Optional. The primary emotions are `neutral`, `calm`, `angry`, `content`, `sad` and `scared`, and many more are allowed (e.g., `happy`, `excited`, `curious`, `sarcastic`). If omitted, the model infers emotion from the transcript.\n\n## Example\nThe page has no full example request. This one is assembled from the schema's defaults and example values:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.cartesia.ai/tts/bytes \\\n  -H \"Cartesia-Version: 2026-08-14\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $CARTESIA_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"model_id\": \"sonic-3.6\",\n    \"transcript\": \"Hi there, it'\\''s awesome to meet you.\",\n    \"voice\": {\"id\": \"db6b0ed5-d5d3-463d-ae85-518a07d3c2b4\"},\n    \"language\": \"en\",\n    \"output_format\": {\"container\": \"wav\", \"encoding\": \"pcm_s16le\", \"sample_rate\": 44100},\n    \"generation_config\": {\"speed\": 1.0, \"volume\": 1.0, \"emotion\": \"calm\"}\n  }' --output out.wav\n```\n\nThe extra context about Baste configuration isn't related to the Cartesia API, so I left it out."}]},"uuid":"e9c472a2-172a-44e0-9885-79401218dbd8","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:45:14.104Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":11959,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Cartesia TTS (Bytes)\n\n**Endpoint:** `POST https://api.cartesia.ai/tts/bytes`. It returns streamed audio bytes (`audio/*`, binary).\n\n## Required headers\n- **`Cartesia-Version`**: The only allowed value, and the default, is `2026-08-14`.\n- **`Authorization: Bearer <token>`**: Use either an API key (`sk_car_...`, from play.cartesia.ai/keys) or a short-lived JWT access token for client-side use.\n- **`Content-Type: application/json`**\n\n## Request body\n\n**Required fields:** `model_id`, `transcript`, `voice`, `output_format`\n\n- **`model_id`**: One of `sonic-3.6` (default), `sonic-3.5`, `sonic-3` or `sonic-latest`.\n- **`transcript`**: A string. The default is \"Hi there, it's awesome to meet you.\"\n- **`voice`**: Either a voice ID string or an object with a required `id`. The docs note that \"Embeddings are not accepted in this API version.\"\n- **`output_format`**: Choose one of these containers:\n  - **`wav`**: `encoding` (default `pcm_s16le`) and `sample_rate` (default 44100).\n  - **`mp3`**: `sample_rate` and `bit_rate` are both required. `bit_rate` is 32000, 64000, 96000, 128000 or 192000, with 128000 as the default.\n  - **`raw`**: `encoding` and `sample_rate` are both required.\n  - **Encodings:** `pcm_f32le`, `pcm_s16le`, `pcm_mulaw`, `pcm_alaw`.\n  - **Sample rates:** 8000, 16000, 22050, 24000, 44100, 48000.\n- **`language` / `locale`** (optional): Accepts codes like `en` or `en-GB`. Use only one of the two: \"setting both returns a 400 error.\"\n- **`accent`** (optional): Normally not needed. Use it only to give a multilingual voice an accent. The value must be one of the voice's listed `accents`.\n- **`normalization`** (optional): `auto` (default), `off`, or a language/locale code.\n- **`pronunciation_dict_id`** (optional): Works with `sonic-3` and newer models.\n- **`generation_config`** (optional, `sonic-3` and newer):\n  - **`volume`**: 0.5 to 2.0, default 1.\n  - **`speed`**: 0.6 to 1.5, default 1.\n  - **`emotion`**: Optional. The primary emotions are `neutral`, `calm`, `angry`, `content`, `sad` and `scared`, and many more are allowed (e.g., `happy`, `excited`, `curious`, `sarcastic`). If omitted, the model infers emotion from the transcript.\n\n## Example\nThe page has no full example request. This one is assembled from the schema's defaults and example values:\n\n```bash\ncurl -X POST https://api.cartesia.ai/tts/bytes \\\n  -H \"Cartesia-Version: 2026-08-14\" \\\n  -H \"Authorization: Bearer $CARTESIA_API_KEY\" \\\n  -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n  -d '{\n    \"model_id\": \"sonic-3.6\",\n    \"transcript\": \"Hi there, it'\\''s awesome to meet you.\",\n    \"voice\": {\"id\": \"db6b0ed5-d5d3-463d-ae85-518a07d3c2b4\"},\n    \"language\": \"en\",\n    \"output_format\": {\"container\": \"wav\", \"encoding\": \"pcm_s16le\", \"sample_rate\": 44100},\n    \"generation_config\": {\"speed\": 1.0, \"volume\": 1.0, \"emotion\": \"calm\"}\n  }' --output out.wav\n```\n\nThe extra context about Baste configuration isn't related to the Cartesia API, so I left it out.","durationMs":12584,"url":"https://docs.cartesia.ai/api-reference/tts/bytes"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bbb72041-49f1-412a-9782-50bce1ae36d0","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
