{"parentUuid":"21dda63f-0428-4609-9780-51dde0abb7e1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1N1pSoyBK5F3KpzuFDf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I need to pick a narration voice from the options—Lauren, Marian, Toby, or Sebastian. Since I can't actually listen to samples, I'll just go with Lauren's expressive storytelling tone and mention the alternatives in case the user prefers something else.\n\nFor revoicing, the tricky part is the tour: scene timing comes from timing.json and words.json, with build.mjs hard-coding absolute segment times based on those word timings. If the new voice changes line durations, those hard-coded times would shift and break the composition, so the safer path is to keep scene slot durations fixed and use Cartesia's speed control to fit the new voice into the existing timing, letting word-level timing (and thus camera moves) adjust naturally within scenes without breaking anything. I should check narrate-tour.mjs to confirm how it actually computes and locks in timing.\n\nBeyond the tour, there's also the studio guide narration (current-narrated.mp4, via narrate-studio-guide.mjs) and walkthrough-en.mp4, an older narrated tour whose source I need to track down — possibly also ElevenLabs — while the French versions of these stay untouched since the user only asked about English. I should clarify whether \"preview\" refers to the landing page tour and \"walkthroughs\" to the guide recordings, as opposed to any persona voice work, before digging into narrate-tour.mjs itself.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":207652,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"output_tokens":898,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":749},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_inp