{"parentUuid":"46c823a2-d7b7-4b62-b0e5-eb56d02d1332","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"deferred_tools_record","entries":[],"toolInputCopies":[{"id":"toolu_0121nSRByAoZfwbHVibunJZc","copy":"wire"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"33a77393-08e6-4e38-ae22-70e20c908219","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:46:22.332Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"33a77393-08e6-4e38-ae22-70e20c908219","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1N4vrcuhe6JvdBywrLY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This walkthrough video has recovered audio but no source script or paragraph-level timing, so revoicing means detecting silences to identify where each paragraph starts, then placing the new Cartesia audio at those points with speed adjustments to fit, and simply swapping out the entire audio track since there's no separate silent video track to preserve.\n\nSo I'm looking at three English deliverables total: the Tour, the narrated Current Studio clip, and this walkthrough video. I'll build a shared helper for fitting generated speech into fixed time slots — generate at normal speed first, then regenerate slower or faster if it overshoots the max duration, with ffmpeg tempo adjustment as a last resort fallback, retrying a couple times before giving up.\n\nFor voice selection, since the user disliked the previous female American voice, I'm leaning toward a British male narrator like Toby to match the \"atelier\" branding feel, though I'll also prepare samples of a few other voices (Lauren, Gemma, Archie) so the user can choose. I'll default to Toby and write the helper script to test speed ranges via trial since I don't have the exact documentation on hand.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1349,"cache_read_input_tokens":307471,"output_tokens":803,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":651},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1349,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":803,"cache_read_input_tokens":307471,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1349,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1349},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":11742,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"1a5c56a7-516f-4622-ba2c-4c7ae2cc3dfe","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:46:22.331Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"1a5c56a7-516f-4622-ba2c-4c7ae2cc3dfe","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1N4vrcuhe6JvdBywrLY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013n8GFMicmCgfKJsZHaKMUy","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://docs.cartesia.ai/api-reference/tts/bytes","prompt":"Exact allowed values/ranges for generation_config.speed, volume, emotion; output_format options for mp3 (bit_rate etc.); any limits. Quote precisely."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1349,"cache_read_input_tokens":307471,"output_tokens":803,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":651},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1349,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":803,"cache_read_input_tokens":307471,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1349,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1349},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_013n8GFMicmCgfKJsZHaKMUy":{"url":"https://docs.cartesia.ai/api-reference/tts/bytes","prompt":"Exact allowed values/ranges for generation_config.speed, volume, emotion; output_format options for mp3 (bit_rate etc.); any limits. Quote precisely."}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"6d06d0e9-a349-4e94-8fc5-adf266364163","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:46:22.335Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"6d06d0e9-a349-4e94-8fc5-adf266364163","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1165d7a1-30cf-4c4e-a93c-fed0ec3c3592","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013n8GFMicmCgfKJsZHaKMUy","type":"tool_result","content":"# Cartesia `/tts/bytes`: allowed values and limits\n\n## `generation_config`\nThis only works on newer models: \"Available on `sonic-3` and newer models; not available on earlier models.\"\n\n- **`speed`** is a double with a default of 1. The spec says: \"Valid values are between [0.6, 1.5] inclusive.\"\n- **`volume`** is a double with a default of 1. The spec says: \"Valid values are between [0.5, 2.0] inclusive.\"\n- **`emotion`** is optional and has no default. If you leave it out, \"the model interprets the emotional subtext of the transcript.\" The spec says: \"The primary emotions are `neutral`, `calm`, `angry`, `content`, `sad`, `scared`.\" The full list of allowed values is: neutral, happy, excited, enthusiastic, elated, euphoric, triumphant, amazed, surprised, flirtatious, curious, content, peaceful, serene, calm, grateful, affectionate, trust, sympathetic, anticipation, mysterious, angry, mad, outraged, frustrated, agitated, threatened, disgusted, contempt, envious, sarcastic, ironic, sad, dejected, melancholic, disappointed, hurt, guilty, bored, tired, rejected, nostalgic, wistful, apologetic, hesitant, insecure, confused, resigned, anxious, panicked, alarmed, scared, proud, confident, distant, skeptical, contemplative, determined.\n\n## `output_format`\nYou must set `container` to `wav`, `mp3` or `raw`.\n\n- **mp3:** Both `sample_rate` and `bit_rate` are required.\n  - `bit_rate` can be 32000, 64000, 96000, 128000 or 192000. The default is 128000.\n  - `sample_rate` can be 8000, 16000, 22050, 24000, 44100 or 48000. The default is 44100.\n  - The spec is inconsistent here: it gives defaults for both fields but also marks them as required.\n- **wav:** `encoding` defaults to `pcm_s16le` and `sample_rate` defaults to 44100. The sample rates are the same as for mp3.\n- **raw:** Both `encoding` and `sample_rate` are required.\n- **Allowed encodings:** `pcm_f32le`, `pcm_s16le`, `pcm_mulaw`, `pcm_alaw`.\n\n## Other limits and rules\n- **Required fields:** `model_id`, `transcript`, `voice` and `output_format`.\n- **`model_id`:** Must be `sonic-3.6` (the default), `sonic-3.5`, `sonic-3` or `sonic-latest`.\n- **`language` and `locale`:** Use only one, because \"setting both returns a 400 error.\"\n- **`voice`:** \"Embeddings are not accepted in this API version.\"\n- **`pronunciation_dict_id`:** Only works with `sonic-3` and newer models.\n- **`Cartesia-Version` header:** Required, and `2026-08-14` is the only allowed value.\n- **Not covered by the page:** It gives no limit on transcript length and no rate limits."}]},"uuid":"397c3a92-ade6-47a2-b691-6b62618c3744","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:46:34.661Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":11959,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Cartesia `/tts/bytes`: allowed values and limits\n\n## `generation_config`\nThis only works on newer models: \"Available on `sonic-3` and newer models; not available on earlier models.\"\n\n- **`speed`** is a double with a default of 1. The spec says: \"Valid values are between [0.6, 1.5] inclusive.\"\n- **`volume`** is a double with a default of 1. The spec says: \"Valid values are between [0.5, 2.0] inclusive.\"\n- **`emotion`** is optional and has no default. If you leave it out, \"the model interprets the emotional subtext of the transcript.\" The spec says: \"The primary emotions are `neutral`, `calm`, `angry`, `content`, `sad`, `scared`.\" The full list of allowed values is: neutral, happy, excited, enthusiastic, elated, euphoric, triumphant, amazed, surprised, flirtatious, curious, content, peaceful, serene, calm, grateful, affectionate, trust, sympathetic, anticipation, mysterious, angry, mad, outraged, frustrated, agitated, threatened, disgusted, contempt, envious, sarcastic, ironic, sad, dejected, melancholic, disappointed, hurt, guilty, bored, tired, rejected, nostalgic, wistful, apologetic, hesitant, insecure, confused, resigned, anxious, panicked, alarmed, scared, proud, confident, distant, skeptical, contemplative, determined.\n\n## `output_format`\nYou must set `container` to `wav`, `mp3` or `raw`.\n\n- **mp3:** Both `sample_rate` and `bit_rate` are required.\n  - `bit_rate` can be 32000, 64000, 96000, 128000 or 192000. The default is 128000.\n  - `sample_rate` can be 8000, 16000, 22050, 24000, 44100 or 48000. The default is 44100.\n  - The spec is inconsistent here: it gives defaults for both fields but also marks them as required.\n- **wav:** `encoding` defaults to `pcm_s16le` and `sample_rate` defaults to 44100. The sample rates are the same as for mp3.\n- **raw:** Both `encoding` and `sample_rate` are required.\n- **Allowed encodings:** `pcm_f32le`, `pcm_s16le`, `pcm_mulaw`, `pcm_alaw`.\n\n## Other limits and rules\n- **Required fields:** `model_id`, `transcript`, `voice` and `output_format`.\n- **`model_id`:** Must be `sonic-3.6` (the default), `sonic-3.5`, `sonic-3` or `sonic-latest`.\n- **`language` and `locale`:** Use only one, because \"setting both returns a 400 error.\"\n- **`voice`:** \"Embeddings are not accepted in this API version.\"\n- **`pronunciation_dict_id`:** Only works with `sonic-3` and newer models.\n- **`Cartesia-Version` header:** Required, and `2026-08-14` is the only allowed value.\n- **Not covered by the page:** It gives no limit on transcript length and no rate limits.","durationMs":12323,"url":"https://docs.cartesia.ai/api-reference/tts/bytes"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6d06d0e9-a349-4e94-8fc5-adf266364163","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"397c3a92-ade6-47a2-b691-6b62618c3744","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1N75V5aL4DmuPzNg926","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I should generate audition samples with a few candidate voices so the user can hear options, then pick a suitable one myself since the request was just to switch to Cartesia. Good candidates include Lauren, Marian, Nandi, and Sebastian — I'll lean toward a voice similar in tone to Aria.\n\nI'll set up a shared Cartesia helper module that both the narration and whisper scripts can use, pick Marian for its calm, steady narration quality that fits the project's tone, and note the user can swap voices via an environment variable if they prefer something else. I also need to double check how the cached segment timings interact with the hardcoded start times in the build script, since switching TTS providers could shift word-level timing.\n\nNew voice durations could throw off the hand-tuned scene starts, so I think the fix is to add a fit mode to the narration script that holds the existing scene timing fixed and stretches each new audio line with ffmpeg's atempo to match the old slot duration, while letting word-level camera cues still follow the recomputed Whisper timings automatically since they're derived from the new audio itself.\n\nThe word cache needs to key on voice too, not just text, since .words.json currently only tracks text. The studio-guide preview script also needs rework to use Cartesia and check voice in its caching logic. For the English walkthrough video, I'd need to recover the transcript paragraphs and caption timings to re-voice it properly, extracting the original video and regenerating each caption segment.\n\nFor actually replacing the audio: I'd check whether the original track has music mixed in or is voice-only, then for each cue in captions-en.vtt generate TTS and place it at the cue's start time, using atempo to compress it if it runs longer than the cue duration. The in-app companion voice isn't part of this since the user only mentioned preview and walkthroughs, so I'll leave that alone. Next I should look at the actual structure of captions-en.vtt.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":215530,"cache_read_input_tokens":92841,"output_tokens":1875,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1673},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":215530,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1875,"cache_read_input_tokens":92841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":215530,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":215530},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":22813,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"3c8ee01a-d363-492f-9450-68e2da94d6b3","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:47:03.465Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
