{"parentUuid":"c01f4485-4239-47ab-963e-8e0fdcb43e27","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1165d7a1-30cf-4c4e-a93c-fed0ec3c3592","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"Exit code 1\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE Narrated edition. Aligned to fal ElevenLabs character timestamps; natural voice speed; actual captured screens with explicit final-frame holds.\n\n1\n00:00:00.406 --> 00:00:03.499\nMake an interface feel like it belongs to someone.\n\n2\n00:00:04.458 --> 00:00:10.035\nIn Baste, start with a persona’s films, music, spaces and working habits.\n\n3\n00:00:10.437 --> 00:00:15.132\nThe fitting makes that world visible through colour, type and interface details.\n\n4\n00:00:15.453 --> 00:00:18.162\nTailor a copy or measure a new persona.\n\n5\n00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:20.507\nGive it a name and a clear description.\n\n6\n00:00:21.037 --> 00:00:25.511\nAdd concrete influences, values and software preferences.\n\n7\n00:00:26.006 --> 00:00:28.971\nChoose the aesthetic axes and visual keywords.\n\n8\n00:00:29.443 --> 00:00:35.182\nSave deliberately; the completion meter measures filled fields, not design quality.\n\n9\n00:00:35.654 --> 00:00:41.377\nIn Tokens, compare spacing, edges and motion, then export CSS, Tailwind,\n\n10\n00:00:41.377 --> 00:00:42.763\nPanda or JSON.\n\n11\n00:00:43.235 --> 00:00:45.642\nDownloaded files stay on your device.\n\n12\n00:00:45.986 --> 00:00:51.900\nThe demo uses built-in token examples; custom measurements do not start fresh generation.\n\n13\n00:00:52.326 --> 00:00:56.463\nBuild a moodboard from image references, tags and notes.\n\n14\n00:00:56.958 --> 00:01:01.223\nPin the important references; leave the notes field to save it.\n\n15\n00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:06.560\nIn Taste, name an asset, explain your verdict and ask for more or less of\n\n16\n00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:07.446\nthat style.\n\n17\n00:01:07.755 --> 00:01:10.999\nInspect the feedback that later prompts can use.\n\n18\n00:01:11.412 --> 00:01:15.201\nStart Generate with a dry run and inspect the prompt.\n\n19\n00:01:15.604 --> 00:01:19.427\nThis browser demo simulates jobs and makes no paid calls.\n\n20\n00:01:19.632 --> 00:01:22.225\nOpenPencil edits a separate document.\n\n21\n00:01:22.628 --> 00:01:28.003\nReal generation, website decomposition, native files and saved projects need the\n\n22\n00:01:28.003 --> 00:01:30.736\nappropriate server or account connection.\n\n23\n00:01:31.323 --> 00:01:36.483\nExplore the material room, save a recipe and reload it when you want another fitting.\n\n24\n00:01:37.279 --> 00:01:43.096\nRemember: reloading Studio clears demo work, while downloads and\n\n25\n00:01:43.096 --> 00:01:45.294\nmaterial preferences survive.\n\n26\n00:01:45.662 --> 00:01:51.188\nThe full English and French guide documents every screen, export and connection\n\n27\n00:01:51.188 --> 00:01:51.889\nboundary.\nArgument 'walkthrough-fr.mp4' provided as input filename, but 'walkthrough-en.mp4' was already specified.","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TqossZupndMVBzSxGPFJ67"}]},"uuid":"df97dd4e-e495-4266-93e3-97c9806225c7","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:47:03.527Z","toolUseResult":"Error: Exit code 1\nWEBVTT\n\nNOTE Narrated edition. Aligned to fal ElevenLabs character timestamps; natural voice speed; actual captured screens with explicit final-frame holds.\n\n1\n00:00:00.406 --> 00:00:03.499\nMake an interface feel like it belongs to someone.\n\n2\n00:00:04.458 --> 00:00:10.035\nIn Baste, start with a persona’s films, music, spaces and working habits.\n\n3\n00:00:10.437 --> 00:00:15.132\nThe fitting makes that world visible through colour, type and interface details.\n\n4\n00:00:15.453 --> 00:00:18.162\nTailor a copy or measure a new persona.\n\n5\n00:00:18.367 --> 00:00:20.507\nGive it a name and a clear description.\n\n6\n00:00:21.037 --> 00:00:25.511\nAdd concrete influences, values and software preferences.\n\n7\n00:00:26.006 --> 00:00:28.971\nChoose the aesthetic axes and visual keywords.\n\n8\n00: