{"parentUuid":"d25c64f2-a4a5-447b-a408-4675176c9635","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"environment","snapshot":{"workingDirectory":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","isWorktree":false,"isGitRepo":true,"additionalWorkingDirectories":["/home/diogenes/.t3/userdata/attachments"],"platform":"linux","shell":"bash","osVersion":"Linux 6.19.14-108.fc42.x86_64"},"changes":[{"field":"workingDirectory","from":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/site/public/media/studio-guide"}]},"type":"attachment","uuid":"414c1d4b-d4e8-4b47-94c8-cb44fe5379b7","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:48:10.753Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n# Environment update\n - Primary working directory: /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste (was /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/site/public/media/studio-guide)\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"414c1d4b-d4e8-4b47-94c8-cb44fe5379b7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1NE99nYkqqkFmKpmL2o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I can't actually listen to audio, so switching to Cartesia means I can't verify voice quality directly—but that's the user's choice to make. The bigger concern is that build.mjs hardcodes absolute segment timings tied to the old Aria recording, so swapping voices will shift scene lengths and break those hardcoded start/end times unless the build re-syncs from timing.json.\n\nMy mitigation plan: generate each new Cartesia line, compare its duration to the old voice duration, then adjust playback speed (clamped within reasonable bounds) and fine-tune with atempo so each line matches the original timing exactly. That way timing.json's scene starts stay valid, while words.json gets regenerated via Whisper so captions and word-lookup cues line up with the new speech.\n\nFor voice choice, I know the user already rejected one option, but since this is more a matter of taste than something blocking the task, I'll just pick a reasonable default (sticking with Bronwen) and mention alternative samples, rather than pausing to ask.\n\nNow I'm laying out the order of operations: update the tour narration script to use Cartesia while keeping fal's whisper for word-level timing, then rebuild and publish; update the studio guide narration script similarly, fixing its caching logic to check for the correct provider/voice metadata rather than just file existence; and finally tackle the longer walkthrough narration, which requires mapping sentences from the walkthrough paragraphs to the original caption timing since some cues split sentences mid-way.\n\nI think the cleanest approach for the walkthrough is to whisper the existing audio via fal to get word-level alignment, cache those word timings, then generate each new sentence and slot it at the original sentence start time, fitting it before the next sentence begins minus a small buffer. I'll start with the tour script first.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2222,"cache_read_input_tokens":315115,"output_tokens":3847,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1548},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2222,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3847,"cache_read_input_tokens":315115,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2222},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":20466,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"90636b9a-1dda-4e78-9a0b-f0455ab01c65","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:48:36.004Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"90636b9a-1dda-4e78-9a0b-f0455ab01c65","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1NE99nYkqqkFmKpmL2o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm selecting Bronwen based on her calm, confident description since I can't preview audio myself—the other five samples remain in /tmp/cartesia-samples/ if you want to swap. Since the video is cut to the old narration's timing, I'll fit each new line to match the original duration using Cartesia's speed control plus tempo correction, then re-time captions word by word.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2222,"cache_read_input_tokens":315115,"output_tokens":3847,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1548},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2222,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3847,"cache_read_input_tokens":315115,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2222},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":1,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":1,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"8627bf9d-1d99-4bd4-8217-930511b86bd8","timestamp":"2026-10-14T02:48:36.009Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"8627bf9d-1d99-4bd4-8217-930511b86bd8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1NE99nYkqqkFmKpmL2o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LmH6vaByKqXXj6hv5piZS9","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='scripts/narrate-tour.mjs'; s=open(p).read()\ndef rep(old,new):\n    global s\n    assert s.count(old)==1, old[:80]\n    s=s.replace(old,new)\nrep('''/**\n * Narrate the Baste tour (videos/baste-tour) with fal TTS.\n * Lines come from videos/baste-tour/SCRIPT.md; each is generated once and cached.\n * Writes narration/<id>.mp3 and narration/timing.json, which the composition reads\n * to place each scene, then times every word with fal Whisper (narration/words.json)\n * for captions. The credential never enters an artifact.\n */''','''/**\n * Narrate the Baste tour (videos/baste-tour) with Cartesia Sonic (scripts/cartesia.mjs).\n * Lines come from videos/baste-tour/SCRIPT.md; each is generated once and cached.\n * Writes narration/<id>.mp3 and narration/timing.json, which the composition reads\n * to place each scene, then times every word with fal Whisper (narration/words.json)\n * for captions. Credentials never enter an artifact.\n *\n *   node scripts/narrate-tour.mjs --skate               # keys from Skate\n *   node scripts/narrate-tour.mjs --skate --keep-timing # fit new lines to the current cut\n *\n * --keep-timing keeps every scene where narration/timing.json has it, and fits each\n * new line to the length of the line it replaces, so build.mjs's edit still lands.\n */''')\nrep('''import { resolve } from 'node:path';\n''','''import { resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { CARTESIA_MODEL, NARRATOR, cartesiaKey, speak } from './cartesia.mjs';\n''')\nrep('''if (!key) throw new Error('Set FAL_KEY or use --skate.');\n''','''if (!key) throw new Error('Set FAL_KEY or use --skate.');\nconst voiceKey = cartesiaKey();\nconst keep = process.argv.includes('--keep-timing')\n  ? JSON.parse(await readFile(resolve(output, 'timing.json'), 'utf8')).scenes\n  : null;\n''')\nold_start = s.index(\"  if (!cached) {\\n    const response = await fetch('https://fal.run/fal-ai/elevenlabs\")\nold_end = s.index(\"  const voice = ffprobe(audio);\")\ns = s[:old_start] + '''  if (!cached) {\n    const slot = keep?.find(scene => scene.id === line.id);\n    let { audio: bytes, requestId } = await speak(line.text, { key: voiceKey });\n    await writeFile(audio, bytes);\n    let speed = 1;\n    if (slot) {\n      // Ask Cartesia for the pace that fills the old slot, then trim the last few percent with atempo.\n      speed = Math.min(1.25, Math.max(0.85, ffprobe(audio) / slot.voice));\n      if (Math.abs(speed - 1) > 0.02) ({ audio: bytes, requestId } = await speak(line.text, { key: voiceKey, speed }));\n      const raw = resolve(output, `${line.id}.raw.mp3`);\n      await writeFile(raw, bytes);\n      const tempo = Math.min(1.15, Math.max(0.87, ffprobe(raw) / slot.voice));\n      execFileSync('ffmpeg', ['-v', 'error', '-y', '-i', raw, '-af', `atempo=${tempo.toFixed(4)}`, '-ar', '44100', '-b:a', '192k', audio]);\n      execFileSync('rm', ['-f', raw]);\n    }\n    await writeFile(metadata, JSON.stringify({ provider: 'cartesia', model: CARTESIA_MODEL, voice: NARRATOR.name, voiceId: NARRATOR.id, speed: +speed.toFixed(3), text: line.text, requestId, generatedAt: new Date().toISOString() }, null, 2) + '\\\\n');\n    // The old word timings belong to the old voice.\n    await writeFile(resolve(output, `${line.id}.words.json`), '{}\\\\n');\n  }\n''' + s[old_end:]\nrep('''    cached = JSON.parse(await readFile(metadata, 'utf8')).text === line.text;''','''    const meta = JSON.parse(await readFile(metadata, 'utf8'));\n    cached = meta.text === line.text && meta.provider === 'cartesia' && meta.voiceId === NARRATOR.id;''')\nrep('''  const duration = Math.ceil((LEAD + voice + BREATH) * 30) / 30; // whole frames at 30fps\n  timing.push({ id: line.id, scene: line.scene, text: line.text, start: +cursor.toFixed(3), duration: +duration.toFixed(3), voiceStart: +(cursor + LEAD).toFixed(3), voice: +voice.toFixed(3) });''','''  const slot = keep?.find(scene => scene.id === line.id);\n  const duration = slot ? slot.duration : Math.ceil((LEAD + voice + BREATH) * 30) / 30; // whole frames at 30fps\n  if (slot && voice > slot.duration - LEAD - 0.1) throw new Error(`${line.id}: ${voice.toFixed(2)}s of voice will not fit its ${slot.duration}s scene.`);\n  timing.push({ id: line.id, scene: line.scene, text: line.text, start: +cursor.toFixed(3), duration: +duration.toFixed(3), voiceStart: +(cursor + LEAD).toFixed(3), voice: +voice.toFixed(3) });''')\nrep(\"JSON.stringify({ voice: 'Aria', total:\", \"JSON.stringify({ voice: NARRATOR.name, provider: 'cartesia', total:\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\nnode --check scripts/narrate-tour.mjs && cp -r videos/baste-tour/narration /tmp/narration-aria-backup && cd /home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste && env -u LD_LIBRARY_PATH node scripts/narrate-tour.mjs --skate --keep-timing 2>&1 | tail -20","description":"Switch tour narration to Cartesia, fitted to the current cut, and run it","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2222,"cache_read_input_tokens":315115,"output_tokens":3847,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1548},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2222,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3847,"cache_read_input_tokens":315115,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2222,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2222},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01LmH6vaByK