{"parentUuid":"1060fbd4-3a8b-4c82-a0d5-03de3a3605ef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1NHXuqeLhaFAmEeXjho","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm wondering if the speed and tempo clamps aren't scaling linearly with the Cartesia parameter—checking whether the \"why\" slot timing of 7.98 vs 7.52 means the atempo clamp at 1.15 got hit, and tracing through how tempo is computed as raw divided by slot after clamping.\n\nGiven the math works out to a clamped tempo of 8.2, Cartesia's speed setting might not be effective, or Bronwen's voice is just inherently slower-paced. Rather than forcing an aggressive atempo, I should relax the fit constraint so voice just needs to stay under scene duration minus lead time, and consider switching to a faster-paced voice like Elaine or Theo since Bronwen runs about 20% slower on the sample. I want to quickly test the speed parameter on the fitting line with Bronwen at speed 1 vs 1.25 to see the actual effect.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4088,"cache_read_input_tokens":317337,"output_tokens":1099,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":459},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4088,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1099,"cache_read_input_tokens":317337,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4088,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4088},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":8158,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"d07f89ba-8954-4efb-ae61-77359ab259b5","timestamp"