{"parentUuid":"f5b3204d-e584-4583-a9a8-fb207f824a09","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1NyP59EH6tPrjzJ1diH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm tracking the tile position across frames by computing y-coordinate as 567 plus the shift value, checking where it falls off-screen versus visible depending on timestamp.\n\nI'm thinking through how to build the ffmpeg overlay — rather than a single y-expression, it may be simpler to use piecewise `enable` ranges with fixed y per segment, mapping each frame's output timestamp back to source time (offset by the 6.0 second start) to generate the right thresholds.\n\nI also need to account for the tour's camera arcs (archB, archC) since during archC the visible region narrows, so tiles that are technically \"off bottom\" by my simple calculation might still be marginally visible or hidden depending on the exact camera crop at that point in time.\n\nNow I'm working out the patch geometry: generating small rounded-corner PNG patches sized to cover each tile with a few pixels of inset, computing exact pixel offsets for two tiles, and planning to rasterize the icon SVGs into PNGs using ImageMagick (falling back to a headless browser render if the SVG delegate isn't available), then composite the overlay before the final scale step in the filter chain.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1674,"cache_read_input_tokens":347363,"output_tokens":1342,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":920},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1674,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1342,"cache_read_input_tokens":347363,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1674,"cache_creation":{"ep