{"parentUuid":"fe1d5587-2458-4d55-bdc6-aab27b07b93c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1PjtDaKTLyTUvwpQD5k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Yes, the voice is Elaine via Cartesia, and I rerendered twice—once for the voice change and once for the icons—without altering the voice afterward. The metadata confirms Elaine was used, and the icon rerender kept the same narration, so I can answer confidently.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":264357,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"output_tokens":526,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":107},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":264357,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":526,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"cache_creation_input_tokens":264357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":264357},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":3033,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"c818791d-ba66-494a-a8b9-8b74f0e15b58","timestamp":"2026-10-14T03:08:10.082Z","effort":"medium","perTurnEffort":"medium","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-ts","cwd":"/home/diogenes/Projects/apps/baste/site","sessionId":"69afbb2a-630d-41bd-9b69-0c77564d8af1","version":"2.1.296","gitBranch":"main","slug":"toasty-puzzling-hopcroft"}
{"parentUuid":"c818791d-ba66-494a-a8b9-8b74f0e15b58","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1PjtDaKTLyTUvwpQD5k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes. The tour now uses a Cartesia voice called **Elaine** instead of the old \"Aria\" voice, and I re-rendered it with her. The icon fix came after that, and its re-render also has Elaine. So the published tour (`site/public/media/tour/baste-tour.mp4`) has both the new voice and the new icons.\n\nThe two Studio guide walkthroughs in English were re-voiced with Elaine too:\n- the short one (0:29) was regenerated;\n- the long one (1:53) keeps its picture, with each sentence re-spoken in her voice.\n\nThe French walkthrough still has its original voice.\n\nI picked Elaine myself. She was the closest narration voice that could keep pace with the existing cuts; I compared six voices on timing but not on how they sound. To compare the same line before and after:\n- `/tmp/voice-compare/tour-old.mp3` (Aria)\n- `/tmp/voice-compare/tour-new.mp3` (Elaine)\n\nSamples of the other five voices I tried (Bronwen, Lauren, Marian, Theo, Clyde) are in `/tmp/cartesia-samples/`. If you'd like one of them, or another Cartesia voice, I can switch it in one place and re-render everything (about 5 minutes)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":264357,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"output_tokens":526,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":107},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":264357,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":4,"output_tokens":526,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"cache_creation_input_tokens":264357,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":264357},"type":"message"}],"speed":"