{"parentUuid":"87168304-33fb-4b6a-bf52-364768fe803b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1QbyEaj6V3tUCheMf9N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"You were right: the tour on the site still had the old voice. It now has Elaine.\n\n**What went wrong:** the render with Elaine's voice was fine, but I published to the site before that render had finished. The site was given the previous video, which still had Aria.\n\n**The fix:** I published again from the finished render. `publish.mjs` now refuses to run until the render log ends in `exit 0`, so this can't happen again.\n\n**How I checked:** hashing the video files doesn't settle which voice they contain, because every re-encode produces a different hash even with identical audio. Instead I compared the narration at 0:19 in each version against the old and new voice recordings. The comparison script is `/tmp/voice-compare/which.py`; 1.0 is a match.\n\n| File | Matches Elaine | Matches Aria |\n|---|---|---|\n| Earlier renders (before the icon fix and after it) | 0.03 | 0.98 |\n| Latest render | 0.98 | 0.03 |\n| Site copy, before re-publishing | 0.03 | 0.98 |\n| **Site copy, now** | **0.98** | **0.03** |\n\n`/tmp/voice-compare/tour-new.mp3` has been regenerated from the published tour (different hash from `tour-old.mp3`), so the two clips should now sound clearly different."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":584,"cache_read_input_tokens":367922,"output_tokens":428,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":584,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":428,"cache_read_input_tokens":367922,"cache_creation_input_tokens":584,"cache_creation":{"ephemer