{"parentUuid":"ec880312-37e6-4b0b-8d43-64df3dbcf461","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg1QopMPBwwb6UsNodb6p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes, Cartesia has male voices. I made samples of two, **Theo** and **Clyde**, reading the same two tour lines as the current voices, so you can compare them directly. The files are named by voice and all have different hashes:\n\n| File | Voice | Length |\n|---|---|---|\n| `/tmp/voices/aria-elevenlabs-old.mp3` | Aria (ElevenLabs), the original | 14.7 s |\n| `/tmp/voices/elaine-cartesia-current.mp3` | Elaine (Cartesia), now on the site | 16.7 s |\n| `/tmp/voices/theo-cartesia-male.mp3` | Theo: \"steady, enunciating, confident young male for narrations\" | 15.4 s |\n| `/tmp/voices/clyde-cartesia-male.mp3` | Clyde: \"gentle, measured male voice with warmth and clarity for storytelling\" | 16.0 s |\n\nEach file reads \"Most interfaces are cut for… A person does.\" and then \"Then it fits an interface to them…\". The ffmpeg warnings in the output are only noise from joining the clips; all four files play normally.\n\nTheo is the quickest speaker of these, so he'd fit the tour's cuts most easily. Clyde runs about Elaine's pace, which also fits.\n\nTell me which one you'd like, or ask for more male options (for example a deeper documentary voice such as Damon or Carl). I'll then re-voice the tour and both English walkthroughs and confirm the voice in each published file before telling you it's done."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":274572,"cache_read_input_tokens":92618,"output_tokens":514,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":274572,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input